{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QhwxNxPd15PBgGTCoATxLw","type":"tool_result","content":"# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D22 post-run, 2026-10-22)\n\nWhat the lane might ask next vs what we can already answer. Grammar is always `Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`;\nid `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>`; the registry is `lib.meta` (built-ins = verified/speculative, plus\n`lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` speculative modules ranked in `lib/meta/prebuilt/TARGETS.json`). Check what exists with\n`python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print(sorted(k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'))\"`.\n\n**Status:** `seen Dn` = GM-verified that day (built-in, verified tier) · `prebuilt <module>` = speculative extractor\nregistered (gate passed) · `partial` = some sibling fields registered · `gap` = nothing registered (TARGET name given\nwhen one exists but is not built yet).\n**Tools:** (I) = installed (`.venv/bin/python` import or on the `source bin/env.sh` PATH), (M) = missing.\nIn-window extractors may only import the prebuild gate's `ALLOWED_IMPORTS` (`hctf/prebuild.py:112`: stdlib subset +\n`pefile elftools capstone Crypto androguard pyzipper lib`) and may NOT call `open()` -- so Evtx / regipy / olefile /\noletools / dnfile / LnkParse3 / lief / cryptography / asn1crypto / dpkt / PIL / `sqlite3` / `mailbox` / `wave` are\nworker-only (LLM side) until the allowlist is widened. See gaps `gate-allowlist-*`.\n**Likelihood** reasoning (history, compressed): D1-D8 identity/image/pdf/zip basics; D9-D15 Windows binaries/installers/\nshortcuts/Office (PE x3 days -> .NET -> MSI -> LNK -> OOXML); D16 e-mail; D17 audio + D18 video (one `media.*` stream\nproperty each, ffprobe vocabulary); D19 ELF, D20 Mach-O (thin; raw `0x` cputype list), D21 Android APK (`package`), D22\nJava JAR (`Main-Class`). Since D17 EVERY family lasted exactly ONE day and one field; the flavor's promised depth\n(transcodes, crops, fat slices, clones, nested launchers) was never delivered in any mode. Timed kits are cumulative\n(+1 field/day) with a 5-name sha256 synthesis; D22 Mastery grew to SIX sets.\n**D22 \"Main Character Energy\" = JAR** (`jar.main_class` of one `application-001.jar` -> `arena.evidence.ArtifactMain`;\nid `d22-jar-001-jar-...`, plain fmt `jar`). Flat 4-entry jar (CRLF MANIFEST.MF with Main-Class + Created-By, one Java-8\nclass that matches it, two filler files); identical in every mode/set. The D21-night prebuild `jar-manifest-class-\nversions` answered it in the race probe (~19 s) -- pre-building the NEXT container family's fmt word paid off.\nFlavor: \"Java archives contain libraries, applications, and nested dependencies whose manifests disagree with their\nlaunchers. Determine what is runnable and where execution begins.\" -> unasked siblings: Spring Boot `Start-Class` vs\nlauncher `Main-Class`, nested `BOOT-INF/lib/*.jar` (refs 3 deep), library jars (no Main-Class -> `none`), Main-Class\nnaming a class that is absent / has no `main`, JarInputStream-vs-JarFile manifest disagreement, Maven pom.properties\ncoordinates of nested deps. The lane has walked runnable formats D19-D22 (ELF -> Mach-O -> APK -> JAR) with a \"launch /\nidentity\" field each, so D23-D25 most plausibly: (a) another RUNTIME PACKAGE whose manifest names an entry point --\nPython (PyInstaller CArchive / zipapp `.pyz` `__main__.py` / wheel `entry_points.txt` console_scripts / `.pyc`\nversion), Node (npm `package.json` main/bin/scripts, Electron `app.asar`), WASM (start section / `_start` export),\nDocker/OCI image (config Entrypoint/Cmd), .NET single-file bundle / ClickOnce `entryPoint`, NuGet/VSIX/CRX; (b) a\nself-executing POLYGLOT (shebang-prefixed jar, Launch4j exe+jar overlay, SFX) where magic @0 lies and the zip starts\nlater; (c) a deeper Java field if the one-day pattern breaks (class-file this_class/has_main, Start-Class, nested jar\nnames, signer). Windows DFIR (EVTX/registry/prefetch, all prebuilt) remains the big untouched block for D26-D31.\n\n-----\n## 1. Atlas\n\n| # | Concept / field | Status | Recognition cues | Standard tool / lib + exact call | D16+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Identity: filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | seen D1 (+D15 member roster) | any member; id stem names WHICH member | `hashlib.<algo>(b).hexdigest()`; `sha256sum` (I) | high -- every timed kit |\n| 2 | `file.magic_prefix_hex_N` | seen D2 | first N bytes | `xxd -p -l 16` (I); `b[:N].hex()` | high (carry-over) |\n| 3 | `text.utf8_bom_present` (utf16 sibling speculative) | seen D3 | `ef bb bf` / `ff fe` / `fe ff` | `b.startswith(codecs.BOM_UTF8)` | high (carry-over) |\n| 4 | `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` | seen D4 | `ff d8 ff`; SOFn `ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc | segment walk; `identify -format %wx%h` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 5 | `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` | seen D5 | `89 50 4e 47 0d 0a 1a 0a`; IHDR @12 | `struct.unpack('>II', b[16:24])`; `pngcheck -v` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 6 | `pdf.header_version` | seen D6 | `%PDF-x.y` @0 | `b[5:8]`; `pdfinfo` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 7 | `zip.eocd_total_entries` | seen D7 | `PK\\x05\\x06` last; u16 @+10 | struct; `7z l -slt` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 8 | `zip.central_directory_member_names` (CD order) | seen D8 | `PK\\x01\\x02` walk, name @+46 | `zipfile.ZipFile(io.BytesIO(b)).namelist()` | high (carry-over) |\n| 9 | `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` | seen D9 | `MZ`, e_lfanew @0x3C, `PE\\0\\0` | `pefile.PE(data=b).FILE_HEADER.Machine` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 10 | `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` | seen D10 | opt hdr +16 | `pe.OPTIONAL_HEADER.AddressOfEntryPoint` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 11 | `pe.version_original_filename` (+ `pe.version_*` family) | seen D11 | RT_VERSION, `VS_VERSION_INFO` UTF-16 | `pe.FileInfo[..].StringTable[0].entries` (I); `exiftool -j` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 12 | `dotnet.mvid_guid` | seen D12 | data dir 14 -> `BSJB` -> `#GUID` | `lib.meta.dotnet`; `dnfile.dnPE(data=b)` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 13 | `m