 = first stream of it; MAGIC):\n226\t  52 49 46 46 .. 57 41 56 45 WAV  chunk walk @12 -> `fmt `: tag u16, ch u16, rate u32, bits u16 @+22; 0xFFFE -> SubFormat\n227\t     tag 1 -> pcm_u8/pcm_s16le/pcm_s24le/pcm_s32le (RIFX ..be), 3 pcm_f32le, 6 pcm_alaw, 7 pcm_mulaw, 0x55 mp3 (D17 pcm_s16le)\n228\t  49 44 33 / ff fb|f3|e3 = mp3; ff f1|f9 ADTS aac; 4f 67 67 53 OggS -> OpusHead/\\x01vorbis/\\x7fFLAC; 66 4c 61 43 flac;\n229\t  .. 66 74 79 70 (ftyp) -> stsd mp4a=aac / alac / Opus; mvhd time = s since 1904; 1a 45 df a3 MKV CodecID A_OPUS->opus\n230\t  VIDEO: trak hdlr `vide` -> stsd avc1/hvc1/vp09/av01 w,h u16BE @entry+32 = `<w>x<h>` (D18 320x180); cross-check tkhd\n231\t     16.16 w/h + matrix (rotation), pasp SAR, clap, SPS crop -- may disagree (\"crops\"); stills (jpg/png) = 1 video stream\n232\t  #!AMR amr_nb|amr_wb; FORM..AIFF pcm_s16be (AIFC sowt=le); 30 26 b2 75 ASF wmav2. Truth: tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/.../ffmpeg -i f\n233\t1f 8b 08 GZIP: FNAME if flg&8, MTIME u32LE@4, OS@9, ISIZE last 4 | \"ustar\"@257 TAR: tarfile.open(fileobj=io.BytesIO(b))\n234\t37 7a bc af 27 1c / 52 61 72 21 1a 07 00|01 00   7z (ver @6/@7; 7z l -slt) / RAR4|RAR5\n235\t\"CD001\" @0x8001                   ISO     PVD @0x8000: system id @+8, volume id @+40, creation date @+813\n236\t\"conectix\" last 512 / vhdxfile / KDMV / QFI\\xfb  VHD/VHDX/VMDK/QCOW2   qemu-img info --output=json\n237\t53 51 4c 69 74 65 20 66 6f 72 6d 61 74 20 33 00  SQLite page size u16BE@16; sqlite3 .deserialize(b)\n238\td4 c3 b2 a1 / a1 b2 c3 d4 / 0a 0d 0d 0a  PCAP/PCAPNG  linktype u32 @20; capinfos -M; dpkt\n239\t-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE----- / 30 82 ..  X.509   cryptography x509 load_*; openssl x509 -noout -text -fingerprint -sha256\n240\tReceived: / Message-ID: / MIME-Version:  EML (GM fmt `email`)  lib.meta.prebuilt.eml.eml_value(b, {\"field\": f}); values VERBATIM\n241\t  (Message-ID keeps <>); first hop = LAST Received; threads: References[0] / In-Reply-To; parts: msg.walk()\n242\t\"From \"@0 MBOX: split on ^From , unescape >From | BEGIN:VCALENDAR/VCARD ICS/VCF: unfold CRLF+space, KEY;PARAM:value\n243\tTime: FILETIME 100ns/1601 (/1e7 - 11644473600); WebKit us/1601; PRTime us/1970; Mac/MP4 s/1904; DOS date/time = 2-s resolution, local. Spelling unverified -> prefer ISO-8601 `Z` for `_utc`.\n244\tMagic @0 not PK but PK\\x05\\x06 near EOF = prefixed/self-executing zip (shebang jar, exe+jar, SFX): parse from the tail.\n245\tHex fields: `0x` + lowercase, zero-padded to the STRUCT width (`_u16_hex` 4 digits, `_u32_hex` 8). GUIDs follow source.\n246\tBOM ef bb bf / ff fe / fe ff -> text.*_bom_present. ELF/Mach-O: byte order from the file (EI_DATA / magic), never assume LE.\n247\t```\n248\t\n249\t## Readiness gaps\n250\t\n251\tRanking (D22 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D23-D25 question (runnable-package / launcher / entry-point siblings of\n252\tD21 APK + D22 JAR: nested/launcher jars, class-file entry, prefixed self-executing archives, software packages) with no\n253\textractor (or a wrong-answer bug in an existing one), or a harness blocker that silently fails a whole family of\n254\tprebuilds. TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail` for prebuild items. The D21 APK items dropped to 2 (APK\n255\tlasted one day like every family since D17).\n256\t\n257\t```json\n258\t[\n259\t  {\"id\": \"jar-launchers-nested\", \"concept\": \"Launcher / nested JAR fields promised by the D22 flavor (Spring Boot Start-Class vs launcher Main-Class, nested jars, runnable?)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend fmt jar (aliases java_archive, war, ear, spring_boot). Fields: start_class (`Start-Class`), spring_boot_version, spring_boot_classes / spring_boot_lib (attr values `BOOT-INF/classes/`, `BOOT-INF/lib/`), main_class_is_launcher (`true` iff Main-Class matches `org.springframework.boot.loader(.launch)?.(Jar|War|Properties)Launcher` or another known launcher), effective_main_class (Start-Class when the Main-Class is a launcher, else Main-Class), nested_jar_names (JSON, CD order, every member ending `.jar`/`.war` incl. BOOT-INF/lib, WEB-INF/lib, lib/), nested_jar_count, main_class_entry_name (`a/b/C.class` from the dotted name), main_class_entry_present / is_runnable (`true` iff main-section Main-Class present AND its .class entry exists; library jar -> `false`, main_class -> `none`), launcher_agent_class, premain_class, agent_class, add_opens/add_exports (JSON split on spaces), enable_native_access, sealed, per-entry section names (JSON, `Name:` values after the first blank line), duplicate main attributes (Java's Manifest keeps the LAST put; record both first/last), manifest_entry_index (JarInputStream only sees MANIFEST.MF as entry 1 or 2 after `META-INF/`; JarFile uses the CD, case-insensitive fallback) -> jar_input_stream_main_class vs jar_file_main_class. Also resolve 3-deep refs `x.zip -> app.jar -> BOOT-INF/lib/dep.jar` and `!/` URL syntax in lib member resolution, so nested manifests answer jar.* fields. Pure zipfile + manifest parser (72-byte lines, ONE-space continuation, CRLF/LF/CR, case-insensitive names).\"},\n260\t  {\"id\": \"java-class-entry\", \"concept\": \"Java class-file depth: this/super class, access flags, main-method presence, module-info ModuleMainClass\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt java (aliases class, jvm; also reachable as jar.main_class_* by resolving the Main-Class entry). Constant-pool walk (tags 1 Utf8 u16-len, 3/4 4 B, 5/6 8 B AND two slots, 7/8/16/19/20 u16, 9/10/11/12/17/18 2xu16, 15 u8+u16; modified-UTF-8). Fields: this_class (dotted), super_class, access_flags_u16_hex, interfaces (JSON), field_count, method_names (JSON in file order), has_main_method (`public static void main([Ljava/lang/String;)V`; flags ACC_PUBLIC|ACC_STATIC), main_method_descriptor, source_file (SourceFile attr), major_version/minor_version, java_version (major-44), inner_classes count, kotlin_metadata_present (`Lkotlin/Metadata;` RuntimeVisibleAnnotations). module-info.class: module_name, module_version, module_main_class (ModuleMainClass attr), requires (JSON). Non-class -> `none`. Stdlib struct only.\"},\n261\t  {\"id\": \"prefixed-zip-launchers\", \"concept\": \"Self-executing / prefixed archives where magic @0 is not PK (shebang jar, exe+jar overlay, SFX, zipapp)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt zip (+ jar, pyz, sfx aliases). Locate the LAST valid EOCD from the tail; archive_start = eocd_offset - cd_size - cd_offset (prefix length) ; fields: prefix_length_bytes, prefix_kind (`shebang` if `#!`, `pe` if `MZ`+PE, `elf`, `script`, else `data`), shebang_line (first line, verbatim, no newline), pe_overlay_offset_hex (pefile-free: last section raw end), overlay_magic_hex_8, embedded_archive_format (`zip`/`7z`/`rar`/`cab`), embedded_jar_main_class (reuse jar manifest parse on the shifted zip), zipapp_main_present (`__main__.py`), lfh_offsets_relative (true when CD offsets are relative to the prefix, as `zip -A` fixes). Make every existing zip/jar/apk/ooxml extractor tolerate a prefix (python zipfile already does; the hand EOCD walkers must add archive_start). Routing: if magic @0 is not PK but `PK\\\\x05\\\\x06` occurs in the last 64 KiB+22, treat as zip.\"},\n262\t  {\"id\": \"software-packages\", \"concept\": \"Software/supply-chain packages: NuGet, Python wheel/sdist, npm tarball, Chrome CRX, VSIX\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Package Deal' pun read as software packages. Separate fmts: nupkg (alias nuget): zip with `*.nuspec` (XML ns varies) id, version, authors, description, dependencies (JSON id@range), tags; `[Content_Types].xml` + `_rels/.rels` + `package/services/metadata/core-properties/*.psmdcp` creator. wheel (aliases whl, python_wheel): `*.dist-info/METADATA` (RFC 822: Name, Version, Summary, Author, Requires-Dist JSON list), `WHEEL` (Wheel-Version, Generator, Root-Is-Purelib, Tag list), `RECORD` entry count / sha256 of a named file (urlsafe b64 no padding as stored), `entry_points.txt` console_scripts; sdist tar.gz `PKG-INFO`. npm (alias npm_tarball, tgz): gzip tar `package/package.json` name, version, main, scripts (JSON object; preinstall/postinstall = supply-chain cue), dependencies. crx (alias chrome_extension): `Cr24` @0, version u32 @4 (3), header_size u32 @8, CrxFileHeader protobuf (signed_header_data -> crx_id 16 B -> extension id = hex mapped a-p), then zip manifest.json name/version/manifest_version/permissions/host_permissions/background service_worker; vsix: `extension.vsixmanifest` Identity Id/Version/Publisher + `extension/package.json`. tarfile/zipfile/json/xml stdlib only. D22 note: wheel `entry_points.txt` console_scripts/gui_scripts (JSON `name=module:func`) and npm `bin`/`main` are the 'where execution begins' fields for these formats -- emit them as entry_points / console_scripts.\"},\n263\t  {\"id\": \"synthesis-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file md5/sha1/size ordering, duplicates, timeline\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) answered sha256 order D15-D20 (Files = note + 2 re-picked kit members + the day's new member; order re-rolls per Mastery set; D20 solver carried the dispatch forward -> timed first try; the 409 pre-fetch body listed DIFFERENT Files than the live attempt). D16 AND D17 timed modes both went solver_incomplete because the day's solver lacked the dispatch (D17 Mastery also needed the artifacts root set inside the per-set _solve_pairs worker). D17-night prebuild added equivalence/odd-one-out/thread groupings; non-hash ORDER keys are still open -> see synthesis-order-siblings. D18: Files = note + panel-001.png + installer-001.msi + video-001.mp4; the single worker pre-wired the dispatch -> TT 23 / Mastery 115 CORRECT in-window first try. D19: Files = note + document-001.pdf + shortcut-001.lnk + collector-001.elf; the single worker added an ELF extractor but NOT the synthesis branch -> TT and Mastery solver_incomplete -> offline generalize ported D18's branch. 4 of 5 timed days lost this way: the day's solver must start from the previous day's solve.py. D21: Files grew to FIVE names (note + panel png + managed dll + message eml + mobile-001.apk), same list in all 5 Mastery sets, order re-rolled per set -- never assume a count.\"},\n264\t  {\"id\": \"gate-allowlist-dfir-libs\", \"concept\": \"Prebuild gate refuses installed DFIR libs\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS lacks Evtx, regipy, olefile, oletools, dnfile, LnkParse3, lief, cryptography, asn1crypto, dpkt, PIL, sqlite3, wave, ordlookup. Targets evtx-records (python-evtx) and regf-values (regipy) as written will fail the gate exactly like pe-debug-rich-imports did (import ordlookup). Either widen the allowlist (all are in .venv) or rewrite those goals as stdlib/struct parsers. Also `open` is banned: regipy RegistryHive needs a path -> use a struct nk/vk walker.\"},\n265\t  {\"id\": \"python-pyinstaller-zipapp\", \"concept\": \"Python frozen/runnable packages: PyInstaller CArchive TOC, zipapp .pyz, py2exe/Nuitka markers, pyc versions\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt pyinstaller (aliases pyi, python_frozen) on PE/ELF/Mach-O: find cookie `MEI\\\\x0c\\\\x0b\\\\x0a\\\\x0b\\\\x0e` (last occurrence); 2.1+ cookie = magic 8 B, pkg_len u32 BE, toc_offset u32 BE, toc_len u32 BE, pyvers u32 BE (e.g. 311 -> `3.11`), pylib_name 64 B NUL-padded; pkg_start = cookie_end - pkg_len. TOC entries: entry_len u32, data_off u32, cmprsd_len u32, uncmprsd_len u32, cmpr_flag u8, typecode char, name NUL-padded. Fields: python_version, pylib_name, toc_entry_names (JSON), entry_scripts (typecode `s`, minus pyiboot*/pyi_rth_* -> JSON and `entry_script` = the last non-pyi one), pyz_present, binary_names (typecode `b`). fmt pyz (zipapp): main_present, shebang_line, main_module text first line. Also detect py2exe (`PYTHONSCRIPT` resource) and Nuitka (`KAY` onefile payload / `__nuitka` strings) -> packager_name. Stdlib only.\"},\n266\t  {\"id\": \"oci-container-image\", \"concept\": \"Container images: docker-save tarballs and OCI image layouts (Entrypoint/Cmd = where execution begins)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt oci (aliases docker, container, image_tar). tarfile over the member: docker-save has `manifest.json` = [{Config, RepoTags, Layers}] (+ `repositories`); OCI layout has `oci-layout` {imageLayoutVersion}, `index.json` (manifests[].digest/mediaType/annotations `org.opencontainers.image.ref.name`), blobs/sha256/<hex> (manifest -> config digest). Fields from the config JSON: architecture, os, variant, created, config_entrypoint (JSON list), config_cmd (JSON list), config_working_dir, config_user, config_env (JSON), config_labels (JSON object), exposed_ports (JSON sorted), history_created_by (JSON), layer_count, rootfs_diff_ids (JSON), repo_tags (JSON), config_digest (`sha256:<hex>`). Spellings: keep JSON strings verbatim.\"},\n267\t  {\"id\": \"electron-asar-npm\", \"concept\": \"Node / Electron runnable packages: app.asar archive header, package.json main/bin/scripts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt asar (alias electron): Chromium Pickle header = u32 LE 4, u32 header_buf_size, u32 pickle payload size, u32 json_len, JSON header {\\\"files\\\": {name: {files:{...}} | {offset: \\\"<decimal str>\\\", size: n, executable?, unpacked?, integrity{algorithm,hash}}}}; file data base = 8 + header_buf_size. Fields: file_names (JSON, depth-first sorted paths), file_count, unpacked_files (JSON), package_name / package_main / package_version from the inner `package.json`, integrity_algorithm. fmt npm / node (package.json anywhere, incl. `package/package.json` in .tgz): name, version, main, bin (JSON), exports (JSON), scripts_preinstall/install/postinstall, dependencies (JSON). Stdlib struct/json/tarfile.\"},\n268\t  {\"id\": \"wasm-start-exports\", \"concept\": \"WebAssembly module depth: start function, exports/imports, name and producers custom sections\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt wasm: `\\\\0asm` + version u32 LE 1; section walk (id u8, size LEB128). Fields: section_ids (JSON in order), start_function_index (section 8; absent -> `none`), export_names (JSON file order) + export_kinds (`func`/`table`/`memory`/`global`), has_wasi_start (`_start` export), import_names (JSON `module.field`), import_modules (JSON sorted unique), function_count (section 3), memory_min_pages/max, custom_section_names (JSON), name_section_module_name (subsection 0), producers_language / producers_processed_by / producers_sdk (JSON `name version`), target_features (JSON). LEB128 unsigned decoder; stdlib only.\"},\n269\t  {\"id\": \"jar-signing-osgi-maven\", \"concept\": \"JAR provenance: v1 signature signer, signed vs unsigned entries, OSGi bundle headers, WAR/EAR descriptors, Maven coordinates of nested deps\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt jar: signature_files (JSON), signer_cert_sha256 / signer_subject_cn / signer_serial_hex (reuse lib/meta/prebuilt/apk_signing.py v1 PKCS#7 walk), sf_digest_algorithm (`SHA-256-Digest-Manifest` key prefix), unsigned_entries (JSON: CD members with no `Name:` digest section in MANIFEST.MF, excluding META-INF signature files), osgi_bundle_symbolic_name / bundle_version / bundle_activator / export_package (JSON), war_servlet_classes (JSON from WEB-INF/web.xml, ns-agnostic local names), war_welcome_files, ear_modules (JSON from META-INF/application.xml), maven_coordinates (JSON list of `groupId:artifactId:version` from every META-INF/maven/*/*/pom.properties, CD order), maven_group_id/artifact_id/version for a single one. Stdlib zipfile + xml.etree.\"},\n270\t  {\"id\": \"apk-manifest-siblings\", \"concept\": \"APK binary-AXML manifest siblings of the D21 `apk.package_name` (version, SDKs, components, flags)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 GM verified `apk.package_name` (id d21-apk-001-apk-package-name, exact_text, trim) = <manifest package=> verbatim; lib/meta/apk.py (stdlib AXML walk: ResChunk 0x0003 file, string pool 0x0001 UTF-16/UTF-8 flag 0x100, START_ELEMENT 0x0102, 20-B ResXMLTree_attribute {ns,name,rawValue,Res_value size u16,res0 u8,dataType u8,data u32}) is the reference. New module lib/meta/prebuilt/apk_manifest.py, fmt apk (aliases android, mobile, axml): version_code (int: Res_value TYPE_INT_DEC 0x10 data, or rawValue string), version_code_u32_hex, version_name, min_sdk_version, target_sdk_version, max_sdk_version, compile_sdk_version (+ compile_sdk_version_codename), platform_build_version_code, platform_build_version_name, application_label (inline string; `@0x7f......` reference -> see apk-label-resources-arsc), application_name (class, expand leading `.` with the package), main_activity / launcher_activity (activity or activity-alias whose intent-filter has action MAIN + category LAUNCHER; expanded FQCN), activity_names / service_names / receiver_names / provider_names (compact JSON, manifest order, expanded), exported_component_names, uses_permissions (manifest order) + uses_permissions_sorted, permission_count, debuggable / allow_backup / uses_cleartext_traffic (true/false; absent -> default false/true/none -- document), shared_user_id, install_location, app_component_factory. Attribute lookup BY RESOURCE ID first (resource map chunk 0x0180: versionCode 0x0101021b, versionName 0x0101021c, label 0x01010001, name 0x01010003, minSdkVersion 0x0101020c, targetSdkVersion 0x01010270, maxSdkVersion 0x01010271, debuggable 0x0101000f, allowBackup 0x01010280, exported 0x01010010, usesCleartextTraffic 0x010104ec, compileSdkVersion 0x01010572, sharedUserId 0x0101000b), then by name (obfuscated manifests rename/strip attribute strings). Never import androguard in the hot path (slow); fallback only. Test on challenges/day21/metadata-package-deal/single_solve/artifacts (versionCode 1, versionName 1.0, sdk 23, platformBuildVersionName 6.0.1, label 'Huntress Evidence <digits>', launcher .MainActivity).\"},\n271\t  {\"id\": \"apk-signing-certs\", \"concept\": \"APK signer identity: v1 JAR signature cert + v2/v3 APK Signing Block, cert digests, schemes present\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 flavor 'distinguish rebuilds from clones' = same package, different SIGNER (clone/repack) vs same signer, new versionCode (rebuild). The D21 APK carries v1 META-INF/FIXTURE-.SF/.RSA/MANIFEST.MF AND an APK Signing Block. fmt apk: signature_schemes (JSON e.g. [\\\"v1\\\",\\\"v2\\\",\\\"v3\\\"] in scheme order), has_v1_signature, has_v2_signature, has_v3_signature, signing_block_present, signing_block_size, signing_block_ids_hex (pair ids in block order, `0x%08x`: v2 0x7109871a, v3 0xf05368c0, v3.1 0x1b93ad61, source-stamp 0x6dff800d, verity padding 0x42726577, dependency/frosting ids verbatim), v1_signature_file_names (META-INF *.SF/*.RSA/*.DSA/*.EC in CD order), signer_cert_sha256 / signer_cert_sha1 / signer_cert_md5 (lowercase hex of the DER cert; also `:`-separated uppercase sibling `_colon` as apksigner/keytool print), signer_subject_dn / signer_issuer_dn (RFC 4514 string, also `_cn`), signer_serial_hex, signer_not_before_utc / not_after_utc, signer_public_key_sha256, signer_key_algorithm (RSA/EC/DSA), signer_key_bits, v2_signer_count, v1_v2_cert_match (true/false), manifest_mf_created_by. Locate the block: EOCD -> CD offset; 16 B before it = magic `APK Sig Block 42`, u64 size before that; pairs = u64 len + u32 id + value. v2/v3 signer: length-prefixed signed data -> digests, certificates (DER). v1: PKCS#7 SignedData DER in *.RSA -> certificates [0] -- hand DER walk (no cryptography/asn1crypto in the gate; pycryptodome Crypto.Util.asn1 is allowed). Shares the DER walker with x509-cert / pe-authenticode.\"},\n272\t  {\"id\": \"apk-label-resources-arsc\", \"concept\": \"Resolve `@string`/`@mipmap` references in the APK manifest through resources.arsc (the 'borrowed product name')\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 flavor 'expose the borrowed product name' = android:label (D21 label was an inline string 'Huntress Evidence <digits>'; a variant can make it a reference 0x7f0X....). fmt apk: application_label_resolved (default config value of the referenced string), application_label_raw (`@0x7f0b0001` style or the inline string), app_label_locales (JSON {locale: value} from every ResTable_config), resources_package_name (ResTable_package name UTF-16 128 chars @+12 -- may DIFFER from manifest package = a rebuilt/renamed clone), resources_package_id_hex (`0x7f`), icon_path (resolved res/... path). resources.arsc: RES_TABLE_TYPE 0x0002 -> global string pool -> package chunk 0x0200 {id u32, name[128] u16, typeStrings, keyStrings} -> TYPE_SPEC 0x0202 / TYPE 0x0201 chunks (config, entry offsets, ResTable_entry {size,flags,key} + Res_value). Ref 0xPPTTEEEE = package/type/entry (type and entry are 1-based / 0-based respectively). Prefer the default config (all-zero ResTable_config); else first. Stdlib struct only.\"},\n273\t  {\"id\": \"apk-clone-rebuild-synthesis\", \"concept\": \"Cross-APK clone vs rebuild synthesis (package id / signer / version / label)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend lib.meta.synthesis (fmt synthesis) for ids `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<key>` whose question lists several .apk (or .ipa) members in `Files: [...]` (parse like digest_order; get_bytes per set). Keys to support by id slug / question words: package_groups (JSON object package -> sorted member names, or list of lists sorted by first name), signer_groups (by signer cert sha256), clone_members ('clone' = same package or same label, DIFFERENT signer than the earliest/lowest-versionCode member), rebuild_members ('rebuild' = same package AND same signer, different versionCode/APK digest), borrowed_label_member (label equal to another package's label), version_code_order (names ordered by versionCode asc, tie -> name), distinct_package_count. Emit compact JSON; names sorted ascending inside groups unless the question says otherwise. Uses apk-manifest-siblings + apk-signing-certs extractors; tolerate non-APK members (skip / `none`).\"},\n274\t  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-identity\", \"concept\": \"iOS .ipa identity: Info.plist bundle fields, embedded.mobileprovision, main executable architecture\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 'Mobile packages' (plural) + the lane's one-family-per-day walk -> iOS next is plausible. fmt ipa (aliases ios, ios_app): zip with `Payload/<Name>.app/Info.plist` (binary `bplist00` or XML; reuse prebuilt plist parser). Fields: bundle_identifier (CFBundleIdentifier verbatim), bundle_short_version (CFBundleShortVersionString), bundle_version (CFBundleVersion), bundle_display_name, bundle_name, bundle_executable, minimum_os_version, platform_name / supported_platforms (CFBundleSupportedPlatforms JSON), device_family (UIDeviceFamily JSON ints), app_bundle_name (`<Name>.app`), executable_cpu_type_set (the CFBundleExecutable Mach-O: reuse macho cpu_type_set -> JSON list of `0x%08x`), executable_lc_uuid, has_mobileprovision, provision_team_identifier (TeamIdentifier[0]), provision_app_id_name, provision_uuid, provision_name, provision_expiration_utc, provision_creation_utc, provision_application_identifier (Entitlements application-identifier), provision_get_task_allow, provision_provisions_all_devices, provision_device_count. embedded.mobileprovision = CMS SignedData DER whose eContent is an XML plist: find `<?xml` .. `</plist>` in the bytes and plistlib-parse (no CMS walk needed). Also `iTunesMetadata.plist` (itemId, softwareVersionBundleId, artistName) if present.\"},\n275\t  {\"id\": \"apk-native-abis-dex\", \"concept\": \"APK payload inventory: native-lib ABI set, multidex count, per-dex header, resources/assets\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt apk: native_abis (JSON sorted set of `lib/<abi>/` dirs: arm64-v8a, armeabi-v7a, armeabi, x86, x86_64, riscv64), native_lib_names (CD order), native_lib_e_machines_u16_hex (per .so via elf e_machine), abi_mismatch (dir ABI vs e_machine disagree -> member names), dex_count (classes.dex, classes2.dex, ...), dex_names, dex_versions (from `dex\\\\n0NN\\\\0`), classes_dex_sha256 / classes_dex_checksum_u32_hex (route into prebuilt dex fields for `classes.dex`), has_resources_arsc, asset_names, entry_count, cd_member_names (CD order), zip_alignment_ok (STORED entries data offset % 4 == 0; .so % 4096), duplicate_entry_names (Janus/MasterKey style dupes), entry_dos_times_constant (true when all 1980-01-01 = reproducible build). Also register the `dex.*` prebuilt fields under fmt apk with prefix `classes_dex_`.\"},\n276\t  {\"id\": \"aab-split-bundles\", \"concept\": \"Android App Bundle (.aab, protobuf manifest) and split-APK containers (.apks/.xapk/.apkm)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt aab (alias android_bundle): zip with `base/manifest/AndroidManifest.xml` in aapt2 PROTOBUF (Resources.proto XmlNode{element=1 XmlElement{namespace_declaration=1, namespace_uri=2, name=3, attribute=4 XmlAttribute{namespace_uri=1,name=2,value=3,source=4,resource_id=5,compiled_item=6}, child=5}}) -- hand varint/length-delimited walk, no protobuf lib. Fields: package_name, version_code, version_name, min_sdk_version, module_names (`base`, feature dirs with `manifest/`), bundletool_version (BundleConfig.pb field bundletool{version=2} string), has_native_libs. fmt apks/xapk (alias split_apk): zip of `*.apk` (+ `toc.pb` for .apks; `manifest.json` for .xapk with package_name/version_code/version_name/split_apks[].id; `info.json` for .apkm): package_name (from manifest.json or base.apk AXML), split_names (JSON stored order), apk_member_names, base_apk_name. Route each inner APK to fmt apk.\"},\n277\t  {\"id\": \"macho-fat-slice-sets\", \"concept\": \"Mach-O universal/fat per-slice SET fields (cputype/cpusubtype sets, slice table, fat_arch vs slice-header mismatch)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 GM field `macho.cpu_type_set` = compact JSON list of `\\\"0x%08x\\\"` cputypes (thin -> one element `[\\\"0x0100000c\\\"]`, GM-confirmed; name `arm64` REJECTED). Prebuilt macho.py answers `cpu_type_set` via its scalar `cpu_type` branch (bare string) -- fix in a NEW module lib/meta/prebuilt/macho_sets.py registering fmt macho (aliases mach_o, macos, universal) fields that return LISTS: cpu_type_set / cputype_set / cpu_types (fat: fat_arch order, dedupe keeping first occurrence; also cpu_type_list WITHOUT dedupe; thin: [header cputype]), cpu_subtype_set (`0x%08x` of the RAW cpusubtype incl. capability bits 0x80000000 for arm64e; also cpu_subtype_masked_set with & 0x00ffffff), slice_count (thin -> 1), fat_nfat_arch (thin -> `none`), fat_arch_offsets_hex / fat_arch_sizes / fat_arch_aligns (2^align), slice_header_cputype_set (cputype read from each slice's own Mach-O header at offset), fat_slice_mismatch (true if any fat_arch cputype != slice header cputype; also mismatched_slice_indexes JSON), fat_magic_u32_hex (`0xcafebabe` / `0xcafebabf` fat64: 32-B fat_arch_64 with u64 offset/size), filetype_set, is_universal (`true`/`false`). Fat headers are ALWAYS big-endian; slices carry their own magic (LE `cffaedfe`/`cefaedfe`, BE `feedfacf`/`feedface`). Disambiguate Java class: `cafebabe` with u32 @4 >= 45 (or u16 major @6 >= 45 and @4 u16 minor small) -> not fat -> `none`. Non-Mach-O (ELF/PE/text) -> `none`. Test on synthesized thin arm64, thin x86_64 (0x01000007), fat x86_64+arm64, fat64, a fat whose slice header disagrees, and a Java class.\"},\n278\t  {\"id\": \"ar-static-archives\", \"concept\": \"Unix `ar` archives (.a static libs, universal .a, Windows .lib) members and object architectures\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 flavor 'thin and universal binaries mixed with archives'. fmt ar (aliases archive, static_lib, a, lib): magic `!<arch>\\\\n` @0 (also thin `!<thin>\\\\n`); 60-B headers: name[16] date[12] uid[6] gid[6] mode[8 octal] size[10] fmag `` `\\\\n `` ; data padded to even. Names: BSD `#1/<len>` (name follows header, counted in size), GNU `/` = symbol table, `//` = long-name table, `/<off>` reference, trailing `/` stripped; BSD symtab `__.SYMDEF`/`__.SYMDEF SORTED`. Fields: member_names (JSON, archive order, symbol/longname tables EXCLUDED), member_count, symbol_table_present, symbol_names (GNU: u32 BE count + offsets + NUL strings; BSD ranlib structs LE), member_mtimes_utc (ISO-8601 Z from decimal epoch), member_sizes, member_modes (octal string), member_cpu_type_set (Mach-O object members -> `0x%08x` list, dedupe, archive order), member_e_machine_set (ELF objects -> `0x%04x`), member_coff_machine_set (COFF .obj in .lib -> `0x%04x`). A universal static lib is a FAT wrapper whose slices are ar archives: route `cafebabe` -> slice -> `!<arch>`. Non-ar -> `none`.\"},\n279\t  {\"id\": \"macos-xar-pkg-dmg\", \"concept\": \"macOS installer containers: xar `.pkg`, flat-package TOC, DMG koly trailer\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt pkg (aliases xar, macos_pkg): header `xar!` (78 61 72 21) BE: header_size u16 @4, version u16 @6, toc_length_compressed u64 @8, toc_length_uncompressed u64 @16, cksum_alg u32 @24 (0 none, 1 sha1, 2 md5, 3 other + name); TOC = zlib XML after the header. Fields: xar_version, toc_checksum_alg (`sha1`/`md5`/`none`), file_names (TOC <file><name> paths joined with `/`, TOC order JSON), file_count, distribution_host_architectures (Distribution XML `<options hostArchitectures=\\\"x86_64,arm64\\\"/>` -> JSON list in stored order), distribution_min_os (`<allowed-os-versions><os-version min=>`), package_identifiers (PackageInfo `<pkg-info identifier= version=>`), package_versions, signature_present (TOC <signature>), signer_cert_cn (x509 in TOC KeyInfo, worker-only if cryptography not allowed). Heap files (Distribution, PackageInfo) at heap offset = header_size + toc_compressed + <data><offset>, encoding gzip/bzip2/none -- only zlib/bz2 stdlib. fmt dmg: `koly` trailer in LAST 512 B (BE): version u32 @4, header_size @8, flags @12, data_fork_offset u64 @24, data_fork_length @32, xml_offset u64 @216, xml_length @224, image_variant u32 @0x1E8, sector_count u64 @0x1EC; fields koly_version, data_fork_length, xml_plist_partition_names (plist blkx Name list), sector_count. Non-matching -> `none`.\"},\n280\t  {\"id\": \"macos-app-bundle-plist\", \"concept\": \"Zipped `.app` / `.framework` bundles: Info.plist advertised architectures and minimum OS vs the real binary\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 'identify what truly supports the advertised fleet'. fmt app (aliases app_bundle, bundle, macos_app; also plist fields under fmt plist): inside a zip (or the asked member is the Info.plist itself) find `*.app/Contents/Info.plist` (macOS) or `*.app/Info.plist` (iOS); parse XML or `bplist00` with stdlib plistlib.loads(bytes). Fields: bundle_identifier (CFBundleIdentifier), bundle_executable, bundle_short_version (CFBundleShortVersionString), bundle_version (CFBundleVersion), minimum_system_version (LSMinimumSystemVersion verbatim), architecture_priority (LSArchitecturePriority JSON list stored order), requires_native_execution (LSRequiresNativeExecution bool -> true/false), supported_platforms (CFBundleSupportedPlatforms JSON), executable_cpu_type_set (Contents/MacOS/<CFBundleExecutable> Mach-O -> `0x%08x` list, fat_arch order), executable_min_os (LC_BUILD_VERSION minos X.Y.Z / LC_VERSION_MIN_MACOSX), advertised_vs_actual_mismatch (true if an LSArchitecturePriority arch is missing from the executable's slices; arch names mapped arm64->0x0100000c, x86_64->0x01000007, i386->7, arm64e->0x0100000c/subtype 2). Values verbatim; booleans `true`/`false`.\"},\n281\t  {\"id\": \"macho-fleet-synthesis\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file architecture-support synthesis over Mach-O / fat / ar / ELF / PE members\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend lib.meta.synthesis (fmt synthesis) for ids `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<key>` over the question's `Files: [...]` list (parse like digest_order; get_bytes per set): files_supporting_<arch> / arch_support_files (names whose Mach-O fat_arch/thin cputype, ELF e_machine or PE Machine covers the asked arch: arm64 = Mach-O 0x0100000c / ELF 0x00b7 / PE 0xaa64; x86_64 = 0x01000007 / 0x003e / 0x8664; i386 = 7 / 0x0003 / 0x014c) in Files order unless 'sorted'/'ascending' is said, universal_files (fat with >= 2 distinct cputypes), thin_files, cpu_type_groups (JSON object `0x%08x` -> sorted names), extension_or_name_liars (name says universal/fat/x86_64/arm64 but slices disagree), union_cpu_type_set (first-seen order over Files; sorted only if the text says so), count_<arch>. Archives (`!<arch>`, zip) expand to their object members. Compact JSON; descending only if stated.\"},\n282\t  {\"id\": \"synthesis-order-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Synthesis questions with a non-sha256 key (size/time/duration order, codec grouping)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis*.py (fmt synthesis) for ids `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<key>-order|groups|<x>` over the question's `Files: [...]` list (parse like digest_order; get_bytes per set): size_order (ascending bytes, ties -> filename), md5_order/sha1_order/sha512_order (generic algo from id), mtime_order (zip DOS mtime of each member from the container CD; also embedded timestamps: EXIF DateTimeOriginal, PDF CreationDate, email Date, mvhd creation), duration_order (media duration_seconds), codec_groups (JSON object codec_name -> sorted names), extension_mismatch_files (names whose magic != extension, file order), largest_file/smallest_file, newest_file/oldest_file. Descending only if the text says descending/newest first. Compact JSON.\"},\n283\t  {\"id\": \"macho-codesign-dylibs\", \"concept\": \"Mach-O load-command depth: dylibs, rpaths, entry, segments, code signature, entitlements\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt macho: load_dylib_names (LC_LOAD_DYLIB/LC_LOAD_WEAK_DYLIB/LC_REEXPORT_DYLIB paths, command order JSON), rpaths, id_dylib, main_entryoff_u64_hex (LC_MAIN), segment_names, section_names (`__TEXT,__text`), source_version, code signature: LC_CODE_SIGNATURE dataoff -> SuperBlob `fa de 0c c0` (BE) -> CodeDirectory `fa de 0c 02` identifier, team_id, hash_type, cdhash (hash of the CD blob, first 20 B hex), entitlements (`fa de 71 71` XML plist keys JSON), is_adhoc_signed. Per-slice for fat (slice index or cputype selector). Fixtures: synthesize minimal thin x86_64 + arm64 + fat headers with struct (no macOS toolchain here).\"},\n284\t  {\"id\": \"macho-arch-name-vocab\", \"concept\": \"Architecture NAME spellings for Mach-O / ELF / PE when a field explicitly asks for names\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Only used when the field id says `_name`/`_names`/`_arch`/`_archs`/`architectures` (D20 proved codes default to hex). fmt macho: arch_names / arch_name_set (lipo/`file` vocabulary: 7 i386, 0x01000007 x86_64 (subtype 8 -> x86_64h), 12 arm (subtype 6 armv6, 9 armv7, 11 armv7s, 12 armv7k), 0x0100000c arm64 (subtype 2 -> arm64e), 0x0200000c arm64_32, 18 ppc, 0x01000012 ppc64), cputype_constant_name (CPU_TYPE_ARM64 ...), filetype_name (MH_EXECUTE/MH_DYLIB/MH_BUNDLE/MH_OBJECT/MH_DYLINKER/MH_KEXT_BUNDLE/MH_DSYM), platform_name from LC_BUILD_VERSION (1 macos, 2 ios, 3 tvos, 4 watchos, 5 bridgeos, 6 maccatalyst, 7 iossimulator, 11 visionos). fmt elf: e_machine_name (readelf strings `Advanced Micro Devices X86-64`, short `x86_64`/`aarch64`), e_machine_constant (EM_X86_64). fmt pe: coff_machine_name (IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_AMD64 / short `x64`/`ARM64`/`x86`). Emit the short lipo/uname-style name for `*_name(s)` and the constant for `*_constant`. Never registered under a `_hex` field.\"},\n285\t  {\"id\": \"elf-dynamic-notes\", \"concept\": \"ELF dynamic section + notes (DT_NEEDED, SONAME, RUNPATH, .comment, ABI tag, gnu.property)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt elf (alias binary/linux). Fields: dt_needed / needed_libraries (compact JSON list in DT order), dt_soname / soname, dt_runpath / runpath, dt_rpath / rpath (verbatim or none), comment / comment_strings (.comment NUL-split, verbatim e.g. `GCC: (Ubuntu 11.4.0-1ubuntu1~22.04) 11.4.0`), abi_tag_os (NT_GNU_ABI_TAG desc u32[0]: 0 Linux, 1 GNU/Hurd, 2 Solaris, 3 FreeBSD) + abi_tag_kernel / min_kernel_version (`3.2.0`), gnu_property_x86_isa_needed / x86_feature_1 (IBT/SHSTK), is_stripped (no .symtab -> true), dynsym_count, symtab_count, dynamic_symbol_names (imports, sorted + DT order variants), init_array_count, e_phentsize, e_ehsize, pt_load_count, program_header_types (JSON list in phdr order: PT_PHDR,PT_INTERP,...). Honour EI_CLASS/EI_DATA for every struct (synthesize a 32-bit MSB fixture too). pyelftools is allowlisted; pure struct is fine. Fixture: day19 collector-001.elf (x86-64 ET_EXEC, interp ld-linux-x86-64.so.2, ABI tag GNU/Linux 3.2.0, stripped, no build-id).\"},\n286\t  {\"id\": \"elf-ident-hex-siblings\", \"concept\": \"ELF ident/header fields in the GM `_uNN_hex` grammar + architecture name vocabularies\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 field `elf.e_machine_u16_hex` = raw Elf_Ehdr member, `0x` + zero-padded to struct width, read in EI_DATA order. lib/meta/prebuilt/elf.py already has e_machine_u16_hex, e_type_u16_hex, e_flags_u32_hex, e_entry_hex, ei_class/ei_data/ei_osabi (as names `ELFDATA2LSB`/`ELFOSABI_NONE`), e_type (`2`). Add the hex/width grammar for every header member: ei_class_u8_hex (`0x02`), ei_data_u8_hex (`0x01`), ei_osabi_u8_hex, ei_abiversion_u8_hex, ei_version_u8_hex, e_version_u32_hex (`0x00000001`), e_entry_u64_hex / e_entry_u32_hex (16 vs 8 digits by class; `e_entry_hex` width = class), e_phoff_*_hex, e_shoff_*_hex, e_ehsize/e_phentsize/e_phnum/e_shentsize/e_shnum/e_shstrndx (integers + `_u16_hex`), e_type_name (`ET_EXEC`/`ET_DYN`), plus vocabularies: machine_name (readelf `Advanced Micro Devices X86-64`), architecture / arch (`x86_64`, `aarch64`, `i386`, `arm`, `mips`, `ppc64le` uname-style), goarch (`amd64`/`arm64`/`386`), endianness (`little`/`big`), bitness / elf_class (`64`/`ELF64`). Fixtures: day19 elf + synthesized ELF32 MSB MIPS (e_machine 0x0008) + ELF32 LSB ARM (0x0028, e_flags 0x05000400) + ELF64 MSB s390x (0x0016).\"},\n287\t  {\"id\": \"elf-arch-synthesis\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file architecture / deployment-group synthesis over ELF + PE + Mach-O members\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 flavor 'Linux binaries from several systems have been pooled with Windows executables and renamed data ... rebuild deployment groups' (never asked yet; the D19 synthesis was still sha256-order). Add lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis_arch.py over the `Files: [...]` list (same contract as lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order): classify each member by MAGIC (ELF/PE/Mach-O/fat/other) -> canonical (format, machine u16/u32 hex, bitness, endianness, os). Fields (fmt synthesis, id tail): architecture_groups / deployment_groups (compact JSON list of lists, members in Files order, groups ordered by first appearance; plus object {arch:[names]} variant keyed by uname-style arch), elf_members / non_elf_members (names whose magic is ELF, Files order), odd_architecture_member, machine_order (names sorted by machine value then name), count_<arch>. Treat a renamed non-binary as format `data`. Fixture: day19 TT kit (collector-001.elf, telemetry-agent-001.exe, managed-001.dll + a synthesized BE ELF).\"},\n288\t  {\"id\": \"media-image-as-video-stream\", \"concept\": \"Still images asked through `media.*` (ffprobe opens JPEG/PNG/GIF/BMP/WebP as one video stream)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUG-LEVEL GAP: on the D18 TT kit, lib.meta.answer('d18-video-001-media-primary-video-dimensions', data=camera-001.jpg / panel-001.png) returns ('none','verified') and audio-001.wav returns (None, None). ffprobe reports a still as stream 0 codec_type video: JPEG -> codec_name mjpeg (demuxer jpeg_pipe/image2, pix_fmt yuvj420p/yuvj422p/yuvj444p/gray from SOF sampling), PNG -> png (rgb24/rgba/gray/ya8/pal8/rgb48be/rgba64be from IHDR bit depth+colour type), GIF -> gif (bgra), BMP -> bmp (bgr24/bgra/pal8), WebP -> webp, TIFF -> tiff. Fix in lib/meta/prebuilt (new module media_stills.py registering fmt media/video/av, or extend media_video): primary_video_dimensions(_pixels)/width/height from SOF/IHDR/LSD/DIB/VP8 headers (`<w>x<h>`, same as D4/D5), primary_video_codec_name, primary_video_pix_fmt, nb_streams 1, primary_audio_* -> `none`; an audio-only WAV/MP3 -> literal `none` for every primary_video_* field (absent stream), not None. Fixtures: the kit's jpg/png from any day18 solver case + the bundled ffmpeg -i to confirm the expected spellings offline.\"},\n289\t  {\"id\": \"video-geometry-crop-aspect\", \"concept\": \"Crop / aspect / display geometry of the primary video stream\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 flavor 'originals, crops'. fmt media (+video/av). ffprobe semantics: width/height = decoder output = SPS size after frame_cropping (h264: (pic_width_in_mbs*16 - CropUnitX*(left+right)); hevc conf_win_*), coded_width/coded_height = MB/CTB-aligned size; sample_aspect_ratio `N:M` from pasp (else SPS VUI aspect_ratio_idc table, else `1:1`/`0:1` when unknown), display_aspect_ratio = reduced (w*sarN):(h*sarD) e.g. `16:9`. Fields: primary_video_sample_aspect_ratio, primary_video_display_aspect_ratio, primary_video_coded_width/height/dimensions, sps_dimensions_pixels, stsd_dimensions_pixels, tkhd_dimensions_pixels (16.16 -> int when whole, else 3 decimals), display_dimensions_pixels (tkhd size; swapped when |rotation| = 90), clean_aperture_dimensions (clap widthN/D, heightN/D, horizOff, vertOff), tapt_clef/prof/enof dimensions (QuickTime), mkv_pixel_crop (Top/Bottom/Left/Right) + DisplayWidth/DisplayHeight/DisplayUnit, is_cropped (true when SPS crop/clap/PixelCrop non-zero or tkhd < coded), geometry_mismatch (stsd vs SPS vs tkhd disagree). ALSO: make primary_video_dimensions prefer the SPS-cropped size when an SPS is present (ffprobe), stsd as fallback; document the choice. Fixtures: hand-pack avcC with a 1920x1088 SPS + crop_bottom 4 (-> 1920x1080) and a pasp 4:3 / tkhd 1440 case.\"},\n290\t  {\"id\": \"video-device-provenance\", \"concept\": \"Claimed recording device / producer of a video (make, model, software, encoder, screen recording)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 flavor 'the recording that could not have come from the claimed device'. fmt media (+video/av/mp4/mov). Sources: QuickTime mdta keys/ilst (`com.apple.quicktime.make`, `.model`, `.software`, `.creationdate`, `.location.ISO6709`, `.camera.lens_model`), udta `©mak`/`©mod`/`©swr`/`©too`/`©xyz`/`©day` (2-byte len + 2-byte lang + text), Android `com.android.version`/`com.android.manufacturer`/`com.android.model`/`com.android.capture.fps`, Samsung `smta`/`SEFT`, GoPro `GPMF`/udta `FIRM`, MKV Tags/Info MuxingApp+WritingApp, AVI `ISFT`. Fields: device_make, device_model, device_software, tag_<key> for every mdta key (ffprobe prints mdta keys verbatim as tag names, e.g. `com.apple.quicktime.make`), handler_name (per stream; `Core Media Video` Apple, `VideoHandle` Android, `VideoHandler` Lavf, `ISO Media file produced by Google Inc.`), encoder (stream `encoder` from stsd compressorname Pascal string @entry+50 len<=31, e.g. `Lavc libx264`, `H.264`, `AVC Coding`; container `encoder` from ©too e.g. `Lavf61.1.100`), is_screen_recording heuristics as diagnostics only (no device keys + display-sized odd dims like 886x1920 / 1170x2532 + VFR stts). Answer verbatim strings; absent -> none. Odd-device synthesis goes to video-geometry-synthesis.\"},\n291\t  {\"id\": \"mp4-mov-atoms\", \"concept\": \"MP4/M4A/MOV/3GP atom metadata (voice memos, phone video)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (aliases audio, av, video, mp4, mov, quicktime). Box walk (size u32 BE, type; size 1 -> u64; size 0 -> to EOF). Fields: ftyp_major_brand (4 chars; emit rstrip'ed, plus ftyp_major_brand_raw verbatim), ftyp_minor_version, ftyp_compatible_brands (JSON, stored order), mvhd_creation_time_utc / mvhd_modification_time_utc (v0 u32 / v1 u64 seconds since 1904-01-01 -> ISO-8601 `Z`; ffprobe tag creation_time prints `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.000000Z`, emit that spelling under tag_creation_time), mvhd_timescale, mvhd_duration_seconds (duration/timescale, ffprobe-style 6 decimals), track_count, track_handler_types (JSON soun/vide/text), mdhd_languages (packed ISO-639-2 `und`), udta/ilst tags `©too` encoder, `©nam` title, `©day`, `©xyz` location (ISO 6709 string verbatim), mdta keys (`com.apple.quicktime.make/model/software/creationdate/location.ISO6709`) as tag_<key>. Pure struct; register via lib.meta like media_streams.py. Fixtures: build tiny m4a/mov with hand-packed boxes in the test (no ffmpeg needed). D18 video-001.mp4 (Lavf: ftyp isom/512/isomiso2avc1mp41, udta/meta hdlr mdta keys=[title] -> `Huntress MP4 evidence <12 HEX>`, handler_name VideoHandler/SoundHandler, encoder `Lavc libx264`) is a ready fixture shape; device keys feed video-device-provenance.\"},\n292\t  {\"id\": \"video-geometry-synthesis\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file video/image geometry synthesis (originals vs crops, aspect groups, impossible device)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend lib.meta.synthesis (fmt synthesis) over the question's `Files: [...]` (mp4/mov/mkv/jpg/png members; get_bytes per set like digest_order). Dimensions per file = ffprobe width x height (stills included, see media-image-as-video-stream). Fields/ids: dimension_order / pixel_area_order (ascending area, ties by name), largest_frame_file, aspect_ratio_groups (JSON object DAR -> sorted names), original_files (per correlation group the largest frame; group key = title/mdta correlation id `<12 HEX>` tag, else same duration+frame count), cropped_files (smaller than its group original or is_cropped), crop_of (JSON object crop -> original), odd_device_file (claimed make/model disagreeing with the group's majority or geometry/rotation impossible for the claimed device: portrait phone recording with identity matrix and landscape coded size, screen-sized dims with camera make), rotation_groups. Compact JSON, ascending/name order unless the text says otherwise.\"},\n293\t  {\"id\": \"image-modern-containers\", \"concept\": \"WebP / TIFF / HEIC-AVIF / ICC under an abstract `image.*` fmt\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt image (alias also for existing jpeg/png/gif/bmp fields: image.dimensions_pixels routes by magic to SOF/IHDR/LSD/DIB) + webp, tiff, heic. WebP `RIFF....WEBP`: VP8 (frame tag, 14-bit w/h after `9d 01 2a`), VP8L (`2f` + 14-bit w-1/h-1), VP8X (canvas 24-bit w-1/h-1, flags ICC/alpha/EXIF/XMP/anim), chunk_ids JSON, has_exif/has_xmp/has_icc, animation frame_count. TIFF `II*\\\\0`/`MM\\\\0*`: byte_order, ifd0 ImageWidth/ImageLength/Make/Model/Software/DateTime/Artist, ifd_count. HEIC/AVIF `ftyp heic|heix|mif1|avif`: major_brand, ispe width x height of the primary item (pitm), item count, Exif item presence. ICC (APP2 ICC_PROFILE / PNG iCCP zlib / WebP ICCP): profile_description (desc/mluc), color_space, device_class, version. Answer formats like D4/D5: `<w>x<h>`. D18 flavor 'previews' + one-namespace-per-family drift: build together with media-image-as-video-stream (same dims parsers, fmt image AND media).\"},\n294\t  {\"id\": \"media-codec-params\", \"concept\": \"Codec-level parameters (AAC profile, MP3 frame/Xing/LAME, Opus/Vorbis details) in ffprobe vocabulary\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (+audio/av). Fields: primary_audio_profile (AAC AudioSpecificConfig object type from esds/ADTS: 2 -> `LC`, 5 -> `HE-AAC`, 29 -> `HE-AACv2`, 1 -> `Main`; ffprobe spelling), primary_audio_codec_long_name (ffprobe strings: `AAC (Advanced Audio Coding)`, `MP3 (MPEG audio layer 3)`, `PCM signed 16-bit little-endian`, `Opus (Opus Interactive Audio Codec)`, `Vorbis`, `FLAC (Free Lossless Audio Codec)`), mp3_mpeg_version, mp3_layer, mp3_bitrate_kbps (first frame), mp3_vbr_header (`Xing`/`Info`/`VBRI`/none), mp3_lame_encoder (9-char LAME tag e.g. `LAME3.100`), mp3_frame_count, primary_audio_sample_fmt for compressed codecs (aac/mp3 -> `fltp`, opus -> `fltp`, vorbis -> `fltp`, flac -> s16/s32 by bps). Verify spellings offline with the bundled ffmpeg -i.\"},\n295\t  {\"id\": \"asf-aiff-caf-containers\", \"concept\": \"Other audio containers: ASF/WMA, AIFF/AIFC, CAF, AU, 3GP AMR\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (+audio/av; also fmt asf/aiff/caf aliases). Route by magic: ASF header GUID `30 26 b2 75 8e 66 cf 11 a6 d9 00 aa 00 62 ce 6c` -> Stream Properties audio WAVEFORMATEX tag (0x160 wmav1, 0x161 wmav2, 0x162 wmapro, 0x163 wmalossless, 0x0A wmavoice) + Content Description title/author/copyright/description + File Properties creation date (FILETIME) and play duration; AIFF `FORM....AIFF`/`AIFC` COMM: channels, numSampleFrames, sampleSize, 80-bit IEEE extended sample rate, AIFC compressionType (`NONE` -> pcm_s16be, `sowt` -> pcm_s16le, `fl32` -> pcm_f32be, `ulaw`/`alaw` -> pcm_mulaw/pcm_alaw, `ima4` -> adpcm_ima_qt) + NAME/AUTH/ANNO chunks; CAF `caff` desc chunk (float64 rate, formatID `lpcm`/`aac `/`alac`/`opus`/`ulaw`) + info chunk tags; Sun AU `.snd` encoding 1/2/3/27. Expose through primary_audio_codec_name/sample_rate/channels/container_format like the existing media modules (format_name ffprobe: `asf`, `aiff`, `caf`, `au`).\"},\n296\t  {\"id\": \"xmp-packets\", \"concept\": \"XMP packet fields in any container (DocumentID lineage)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt xmp (also registered under jpeg/png/pdf/media/ooxml/image as xmp_<field>). Find `<x:xmpmeta` ... `</x:xmpmeta>` (or `<?xpacket begin` ... `<?xpacket end`) anywhere in the bytes (JPEG APP1 `http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/\\\\0`, PNG iTXt `XML:com.adobe.xmp`, PDF Metadata stream if uncompressed, MP4 `uuid` BE7ACFCB-97A9-42E8-9C71-999491E3AFAC, WAV `_PMX` chunk). Parse with xml.etree (namespaces by URI, rdf:Description attributes AND child elements, rdf:Seq/Alt/Bag -> lists). Fields: document_id, instance_id, original_document_id (verbatim incl. `xmp.did:`/`uuid:` prefixes), derived_from_document_id, history_actions (JSON, stored order), history_software_agents, creator_tool, create_date, modify_date, metadata_date (verbatim), dc_creator (JSON list), dc_title (x-default), dc_format. Synthesis helper: files sharing document_id/original_document_id.\"},\n297\t  {\"id\": \"subtitle-chapter-streams\", \"concept\": \"Cover art, subtitle and chapter streams (ffprobe stream accounting)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (+av/video). ffprobe counts an embedded cover (ID3 APIC, MP4 `covr`, FLAC PICTURE block, MKV attachment with image mime) as a VIDEO stream with codec_name `mjpeg`/`png` and disposition attached_pic=1 -> fields attached_pic_present, attached_pic_codec_name, attached_pic_mime_type, attached_pic_dimensions_pixels, nb_streams_including_cover (document the difference vs audio_stream_count). Subtitles: MP4 `tx3g` -> `mov_text`, MKV S_TEXT/UTF8 -> `subrip`, S_TEXT/ASS -> `ass`, S_TEXT/WEBVTT -> `webvtt`; fields subtitle_stream_count, subtitle_codec_names (stream order), subtitle_languages. Chapters: MP4 `chpl`/QuickTime chapter track, MKV EditionEntry/ChapterAtom -> chapter_count, chapter_titles (JSON), chapter_start_times_seconds.\"},\n298\t  {\"id\": \"zone-identifier-motw\", \"concept\": \"Download provenance: Zone.Identifier ADS, macOS quarantine, AppleDouble\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt zone_identifier (aliases motw, ads): text `[ZoneTransfer]` INI (UTF-8/UTF-16 with BOM): zone_id (int), zone_name (0 Local,1 Intranet,2 Trusted,3 Internet,4 Restricted), referrer_url, host_url, last_writer_package_family_name, app_zone_id -- values verbatim. Member names like `x.exe:Zone.Identifier` or `x.exe_Zone.Identifier`. fmt quarantine: `com.apple.quarantine` value `flags;hex_unix_time;agent;uuid` -> quarantine_flags_hex, quarantine_time_utc, quarantine_agent, quarantine_event_uuid. fmt appledouble: `00 05 16 07` header, entry table (id 2 resource fork, 9 Finder info with `ATTR` xattr block) -> xattr_names (JSON), xattr_<name> (UTF-8 if printable else hex), finder_type_creator.\"},\n299\t  {\"id\": \"archives-tar-7z-iso\", \"concept\": \"TAR / 7z / RAR / ISO9660-UDF headers (archives gap only produced gzip)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt archives were not registered by the earlier `archives` run (tar/7z/rar/iso have 0 fields). Separate modules: tar (ustar_magic, member_names stored order, member_sizes, member_mtimes_utc, member_modes_octal, member_unames/gnames, typeflags) via tarfile.open(fileobj=io.BytesIO(b)); 7z (signature_version `0.4`, next_header_offset/size, start_header_crc32_hex, has_encrypted_header when the next header is kEncodedHeader with AES coder 06f10701); rar (version 4|5, RAR5 main archive flags, file names when headers unencrypted, is_header_encrypted); iso (pvd system_id, volume_id, volume_set_id, publisher_id, application_id (strip spaces), volume_creation_date_utc from 17-byte dec-datetime @813 with GMT offset, volume_space_size, logical_block_size, joliet_present (SVD escape %/@ %/C %/E), udf_present (BEA01/NSR02/NSR03), root_member_names). fmt `archive` alias for all.\"},\n300\t  {\"id\": \"media-fmt-alias\", \"concept\": \"GM fmt `media` -> prebuilt `wav`/`mp3` fields + D17 codec name in lib\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/media.py registering fmt 'media' (aliases 'audio', 'av') that routes by MAGIC to the existing wav/mp3/gif... extractors, and registers ('media','primary_audio_codec_name') (GM-verified D17: 16-bit PCM WAV -> 'pcm_s16le') by porting challenges/day17/metadata-hear-me-out/solver/solve.py _audio_codec (RIFF/RIFX/RF64, AIFF/AIFC, fLaC, Ogg Opus/Vorbis/FLAC/Speex, AMR, .snd, MP4 stsd, Matroska CodecID, MPEG/ADTS sync). Do NOT change the pcm_s16le mapping. D16 lesson repeated: an extractor under the container's fmt word is invisible to the GM's namespace.\"},\n301\t  {\"id\": \"media-stream-fields\", \"concept\": \"ffprobe-style stream/format fields for the first audio stream\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields primary_audio_sample_rate_hz (also _sample_rate), primary_audio_channels, primary_audio_channel_layout (ffprobe: mono/stereo/2.1/quad/5.1...), primary_audio_bits_per_sample (ffprobe bits_per_sample; 0 for lossy), primary_audio_sample_fmt (u8/s16/s32/flt/dbl; planar 'fltp' for aac/opus/vorbis decoders), primary_audio_bit_rate (bps integer: PCM = rate*ch*bits), primary_audio_codec_long_name ('PCM signed 16-bit little-endian'), primary_audio_codec_tag_hex ('0x0001'), primary_audio_codec_tag_string ffprobe-style, primary_audio_duration_seconds (string with 6 decimals like ffprobe '1.250000'), primary_audio_nb_samples / duration_ts, format_name (ffprobe demuxer: wav, mp3, ogg, flac, aiff, amr, au, 'mov,mp4,m4a,3gp,3g2,mj2', 'matroska,webm'), format_long_name, nb_streams, audio_stream_count, format_duration_seconds, format_size_bytes, format_bit_rate. WAV: data chunk size / byte rate; MP3: Xing/Info/VBRI frames or frame walk; Ogg: last page granule / rate (Opus 48 kHz minus pre_skip); FLAC: STREAMINFO total samples; MP4: mdhd timescale/duration.\"},\n302\t  {\"id\": \"media-wav-deep\", \"concept\": \"WAV chunk-level metadata (BWF bext, fact, LIST/INFO, cue, iXML, data-vs-RIFF size, trailing bytes)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media + wav alias, fields riff_chunk_ids (file order JSON), info_title (INAM; D17 carried 'Huntress audio evidence <12 hex>'), info_software (ISFT), info_creation_date (ICRD), info_comment (ICMT), info_artist (IART), bext_description, bext_originator, bext_originator_reference, bext_origination_date, bext_origination_time, bext_time_reference, bext_umid_hex, fact_sample_count, data_chunk_size_bytes, riff_size_declared, riff_size_mismatch (declared+8 != len), trailing_bytes_after_data (count + magic_prefix_hex_16 of the trailer -> hidden payload), cue_point_count, ixml_present. Pure struct; values verbatim (strip trailing NULs).\"},\n303\t  {\"id\": \"media-renamed-containers\", \"concept\": \"Renamed/transcoded audio: actual container + codec vs the extension\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields container_format (by magic: wav/rf64/aiff/mp3/ogg/flac/mp4/matroska/amr/au/adts/caf/wma-asf), declared_extension, extension_matches_content (true/false), mime_type_by_magic (audio/wav, audio/mpeg, audio/ogg, audio/flac, audio/mp4, audio/amr), plus primary_audio_codec_name for: ASF/WMA (GUID 3026b275 + stream props -> wmav2), CAF ('caff' desc fourcc), MP4 esds objectTypeIndication (0x40 aac, 0x6b mp3), Ogg multiple codecs. Flavor D17: 'Voice notes have been transcoded, renamed'.\"},\n304\t  {\"id\": \"media-multistream\", \"concept\": \"Per-stream fields in multi-stream containers; the odd stream\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields stream_codec_names (JSON, container stream index order like ffprobe), audio_stream_codec_names, stream_languages (MP4 mdhd packed ISO-639-2 / MKV Language default 'eng' / 'und'), stream_titles (MKV Name, MP4 udta name/handler_name), stream_creation_times_utc (mdhd 1904 epoch), stream_durations_seconds, stream_sample_rates, primary_video_codec_name, odd_stream_index (the one whose codec/language/rate/creation_time differs from the majority -- emit index and a JSON diagnostic). MP4 box walk moov/trak/mdia/{mdhd,hdlr,minf/stbl/stsd}; Matroska EBML walk Segment/Tracks/TrackEntry (TrackType 2=audio, CodecID map A_OPUS opus, A_VORBIS vorbis, A_AAC aac, A_FLAC flac, A_MPEG/L3 mp3, A_PCM/INT/LIT pcm_s16le by BitDepth, A_AC3 ac3, V_MPEG4/ISO/AVC h264, V_MPEGH/ISO/HEVC hevc, V_VP9 vp9, V_AV1 av1); Ogg: group pages by serial, BOS packet per stream. Flavor D17: 'find the stream that breaks the sender's story'.\"},\n305\t  {\"id\": \"media-format-tags\", \"concept\": \"Container/stream tags: title, artist, comment, encoder, creation_time, language\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields tag_title, tag_artist, tag_album, tag_comment, tag_encoder, tag_date, tag_creation_time_utc, tag_<key> generic (lowercase ffprobe key), encoder (ffprobe format tag 'encoder': ID3 TSSE, Vorbis/Opus ENCODER + vendor string, MP4 \\\\xa9too, MKV MuxingApp/WritingApp, WAV ISFT), opus_vendor / vorbis_vendor, id3_version. Sources: WAV LIST/INFO, ID3v2.2-2.4 (+v1), Vorbis comment (Ogg/FLAC/Opus OpusTags), MP4 moov/udta/meta/ilst, MKV Tags. Reuse prebuilt mp3/wav parsers where possible; stdlib only (mutagen is not allowlisted).\"},\n306\t  {\"id\": \"email-media-attachments\", \"concept\": \"Audio embedded in mail: MIME audio attachments + member resolution through .eml\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt email (+eml/mime aliases), fields attachment_audio_codec_names (MIME order, via the media codec extractor on decoded payloads), attachment_media_container_formats, attachment_declared_content_types, attachment_audio_mismatch_names (declared Content-Type/extension vs actual codec), attachment_audio_durations_seconds, audio_attachment_count. Also expose lib.meta.prebuilt helper attachment_bytes(eml_bytes, filename) (RFC 2231/2047 filename decode, get_payload(decode=True)) so artifact refs like `message-001.eml -> voice-001.ogg` and `zip -> eml -> wav` resolve. Flavor D17: 'embedded in mail'.\"},\n307\t  {\"id\": \"media-equivalence-synthesis\", \"concept\": \"Cross-recording equivalence / odd-one-out synthesis\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Add to lib.meta.synthesis: equivalence_groups(question, get_bytes) over the `Files: [...]` audio members -> group by (1) shared title/correlation tag (WAV INAM, ID3 TIT2, Vorbis TITLE, MP4 \\\\xa9nam; D17 INAM 'Huntress audio evidence <12 hex>'), (2) equal decoded duration rounded to 10 ms / equal sample count, (3) equal PCM data-chunk sha256 or FLAC STREAMINFO MD5; outputs compact JSON array of arrays of filenames (each group sorted, groups by first name), the odd_one_out filename, duplicate_count. Also md5/sha1/size-order variants of digest_order (synthesis-siblings). Spelling unverified -> keep alternates.\"},\n308\t  {\"id\": \"tool-ffprobe\", \"concept\": \"ffprobe/ffmpeg + sox for media ground truth\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"PARTLY SOLVED: ffmpeg 7.0.2 ships at tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2 (imageio-ffmpeg; not on PATH, no ffprobe). `ffmpeg -hide_banner -i f` prints ffprobe vocabulary (`Stream #0:0: Audio: pcm_s16le ([1][0][0][0] / 0x0001), 16000 Hz, mono, s16`, format tags) -- verified on D17. Still wanted: a bin/ shim `ffmpeg` on PATH and a real ffprobe (static build) for `-show_streams -show_format -of json`; apt sox (soxi). Worker/offline verification only, never in-window. D18: the same `ffmpeg -i` line verified video geometry (`h264 (High) (avc1 / 0x31637661), yuv420p(progressive), 320x180 [SAR 1:1 DAR 16:9], 10 fps`).\"},\n309\t  {\"id\": \"email-fmt-alias\", \"concept\": \"GM fmt `email` -> prebuilt `eml` fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/email.py re-registering EVERY ('eml', f) field of lib/meta/prebuilt/eml.py under fmt 'email' (also 'mail', 'mime') with the same extractor. D16 GM asked email.message_id; the eml-registered extractor was invisible to the solver. Message-ID verbatim WITH angle brackets (GM-verified D16).\"},\n310\t  {\"id\": \"email-threading\", \"concept\": \"In-Reply-To / References / thread root / reply-forward flags\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt email (+eml alias), fields in_reply_to, references (compact JSON list, stored order, each id with <>), references_count, thread_root_message_id (References[0] else In-Reply-To else own Message-ID), parent_message_id (last References id else In-Reply-To), is_reply, is_forward (Re:/Fwd:/FW: prefix or X-Forwarded-*), normalized_subject (strip Re:/Fwd: repeatedly), thread_index_guid (Outlook Thread-Index base64: 22-byte header = FILETIME-ish 6 B + GUID 16 B), thread_topic, resent_message_id, header_<name> generic (first occurrence, unfolded, verbatim). stdlib email only.\"},\n311\t  {\"id\": \"email-mime-attachments\", \"concept\": \"MIME tree, attachment names/sizes/hashes/types\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt email, fields mime_part_count, content_type (top-level, no params), mime_boundary, attachment_count, attachment_names (MIME order), attachment_content_types, attachment_sizes_bytes (decoded), attachment_sha256s / md5s / sha1s (decoded payload), attachment_magic_prefix_hex_16, attachment_declared_vs_magic_mismatch, body_text_sha256, content_transfer_encodings. msg.walk() + get_payload(decode=True); RFC 2231/2047 filenames decoded.\"},\n312\t  {\"id\": \"mbox-collection\", \"concept\": \"MBOX / mailbox export: count, ids, duplicates, threads\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt mbox (alias mailbox), fields message_count, message_ids (file order, with <>), unique_message_id_count, duplicate_message_ids (sorted), thread_count, thread_root_ids, subjects, first_date_utc, last_date_utc. Split bytes on b'\\\\nFrom ' (first line at 0), unescape '>From ', parse each with email.message_from_bytes (stdlib mailbox needs a path -> not allowed).\"},\n313\t  {\"id\": \"email-thread-synthesis\", \"concept\": \"Cross-message threading over several .eml members\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D16 flavor: 'rebuild which mail actually belongs together'. Add to lib.meta.synthesis: thread_groups(question, get_bytes) over the `Files: [...]` list -> group by thread root (References/In-Reply-To, union-find), dedupe by Message-ID, order members by Date then filename; outputs: compact JSON array of arrays (filenames), thread_count, duplicate filenames, root filename per thread. Spelling unverified -> register sorted-filename variant and keep date order as an alternate.\"},\n314\t  {\"id\": \"pe-debug-rich-imports\", \"concept\": \"PE PDB path / Rich header / imphash / imports / exports / Authenticode\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Re-run the REJECTED target without `import ordlookup` (pefile.PE.get_imphash already handles ordinals). fmt pe, fields debug_pdb_path, debug_codeview_guid, debug_codeview_age, rich_header_hash_md5, rich_header_xor_key_u32_hex, imphash, import_dll_names, export_names, export_dll_name. Do not re-register time_date_stamp_u32_hex (exists).\"},\n315\t  {\"id\": \"pe-authenticode\", \"concept\": \"PE Authenticode signer / cert serial / thumbprint / signing time\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt pe, fields is_signed, security_dir_size_u32_hex, signer_subject_cn, signer_issuer_cn, signer_serial_hex, signer_cert_sha1, signer_cert_sha256, signing_time_utc. Data dir 4 VirtualAddress is a file offset; WIN_CERTIFICATE (len u32, rev 0x0200, type 2) + PKCS#7 SignedData. Needs asn1crypto/cryptography in ALLOWED_IMPORTS or a minimal stdlib DER walker.\"},\n316\t  {\"id\": \"evtx-records\", \"concept\": \"EVTX record fields (EventID, TimeCreated, Provider, Channel, Computer, count)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt evtx: record_count, first_event_id, first_time_created_utc, provider_names, channel, computer_name) + event_ids (ordered list), last_event_record_id, event_data_<name> family. Blocked by gate-allowlist-dfir-libs unless a stdlib BinXML walker is written (template substitution makes that ~400 lines; widening the allowlist for Evtx is cheaper).\"},\n317\t  {\"id\": \"regf-values\", \"concept\": \"Registry key/value lookups (Run keys, last-write, counts, UserAssist)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt regf: run_key_values, last_written_utc, subkey_count, value_count, userassist_entries) + value_<path> family, computer_name, timezone_key_name. Use a struct nk/vk/lf/lh/ri walker over hbins (stdlib) since regipy needs a file path and is not allowlisted.\"},\n318\t  {\"id\": \"recycle-bin-i\", \"concept\": \"Recycle Bin $I original path / deletion time / size\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Split from target jumplist-recycle-mft so it lands alone: fmt recycle (also alias fmt recyclebin), fields original_path, deleted_time_utc, original_size, format_version. v1: header=1, size u64@8, FILETIME@16, UTF-16 path 520 B@24; v2: header=2, path chars u32@24, path@28. Pure struct, ~40 lines.\"},\n319\t  {\"id\": \"prefetch\", \"concept\": \"Prefetch exe name / run count / last run times / volume info\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt prefetch: executable_name, run_count, last_run_time_utc, format_version, prefetch_hash_u32_hex, volume_serial_u32_hex) + last_run_times_utc (list of 8), volume_device_path, referenced_file_count. Uncompressed SCCA v17/23/26/30 is struct-only; Win10 MAM\\\\x04 needs an LZXpress-Huffman decoder (stdlib port ~120 lines, or tool dissect.util).\"},\n320\t  {\"id\": \"task-xml\", \"concept\": \"Scheduled task XML (Command, Arguments, Author, Date, URI, Triggers)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt task (aliases scheduled_task, task_xml), fields exec_command, exec_arguments, registration_author, registration_date, uri, principal_user_id, run_level, trigger_types, hidden. UTF-16LE BOM XML, ns http://schemas.microsoft.com/windows/2004/02/mit/task; xml.etree with local-name matching.\"},\n321\t  {\"id\": \"ole-vba\", \"concept\": \"VBA macro project (module names, auto-exec, stomping)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt vba (and ole alias fields), fields module_names, project_name, has_macros, autoexec_keywords, vba_stream_names, code_page. Reuse lib/meta/cfb.py cfb_streams; dir stream is MS-OVBA RLE-compressed (port the ~40-line decompressor, stdlib). Covers .doc/.xls CFB and OOXML word/vbaProject.bin.\"},\n322\t  {\"id\": \"ooxml-siblings\", \"concept\": \"OOXML custom props / remote template / embeddings / internal rel targets\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt ooxml, fields custom_properties (JSON name->value), attached_template_target, internal_relationship_targets, relationship_types, embedded_object_names, has_vba_project, main_part_content_type, hyperlink_count. Mirror D15 conventions (compact JSON, sorted for gathered sets). external_relationship_targets is verified -- do not re-register.\"},\n323\t  {\"id\": \"email-auth-results\", \"concept\": \"SPF/DKIM/DMARC results, ARC, sender mismatch\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt email, fields spf_result, dkim_result, dmarc_result, authserv_id, arc_seal_count, dkim_signed_headers (h= list), return_path_domain, from_domain, reply_to_domain, from_return_path_mismatch, reply_to_mismatch, received_spf_result. Regex over unfolded Authentication-Results / Received-SPF / DKIM-Signature.\"},\n324\t  {\"id\": \"outlook-msg\", \"concept\": \"Outlook .msg (CFB) message properties\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt msg (alias outlook_msg), fields message_id (__substg1.0_1035001F), in_reply_to (1042001F), subject (0037001F), sender_email (0C1F001F/5D01001F), message_class (001A001F), transport_headers (007D001F), attachment_names (__attach_version1.0_#*/3707001F else 3704001F), attachment_count, client_submit_time_utc (__properties_version1.0 0x00390040 FILETIME). Reuse lib/meta/cfb.py streams; UTF-16LE for 001F.\"},\n325\t  {\"id\": \"ics-vcard\", \"concept\": \"iCalendar / vCard fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt ics (aliases ical, calendar): uid, organizer, attendees, dtstart_utc, dtend_utc, summary, location, method, prodid, event_count; fmt vcard (alias vcf): fn, email, tel, org, uid, version. RFC 5545 unfolding (CRLF + space/tab), parameters split on ';', value after first ':'.\"},\n326\t  {\"id\": \"url-library-ms\", \"concept\": \"`.url` / `.library-ms` / `.searchConnector-ms` shortcuts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt url (alias internet_shortcut): url, icon_file, icon_index, working_directory, hotkey; fmt library_ms (aliases library, searchconnector): location_urls (simpleLocation/url), is_library_pinned, folder_type, owner_sid, version. configparser-free line parse; xml.etree local names.\"},\n327\t  {\"id\": \"jumplist\", \"concept\": \"Jump list AutomaticDestinations AppID + DestList + embedded LNK targets\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt jumplist, fields app_id (from member filename), destlist_entry_count, destlist_paths, lnk_stream_names, first_target_path. cfb_streams + reuse prebuilt lnk parser on each numeric stream. DestList v3/v4 entry layout struct.\"},\n328\t  {\"id\": \"pdf-info\", \"concept\": \"PDF Info dict / page count / %%EOF count / Encrypt / JS\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt pdf: info_title ... encrypted) + has_javascript, open_action_present, embedded_file_names, xmp_creator_tool. Handle /ObjStm via zlib. pdf.header_version is verified -- don't touch.\"},\n329\t  {\"id\": \"exif\", \"concept\": \"JPEG EXIF Make/Model/DateTimeOriginal/GPS\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt jpeg: exif_make ... app_segments) + exif_software, exif_gps_longitude, exif_gps_decimal, xmp_creator_tool. Pure-Python TIFF IFD walker (II/MM), GPS rationals -> decimal degrees; spelling unknown -> also store DMS.\"},\n330\t  {\"id\": \"png-text-time\", \"concept\": \"PNG tEXt/iTXt/zTXt/tIME, chunk order, trailing data\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt png: text_chunks, time_chunk, chunk_names, ihdr_bit_depth, ihdr_color_type) + trailing_bytes_after_iend, text_<keyword> family.\"},\n331\t  {\"id\": \"mft-record\", \"concept\": \"$MFT FILE record $SI vs $FN timestamps, name, parent\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt mft, fields file_name, record_number, parent_record_number, si_created_utc, si_modified_utc, fn_created_utc, fn_modified_utc, timestomp_suspected, is_directory, resident_data_hex_16. Apply update-sequence fixups first.\"},\n332\t  {\"id\": \"archives\", \"concept\": \"GZIP/TAR/7z/RAR/ISO headers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt gzip) + separate modules tar (member_names, ustar_magic, member_mtimes_utc, member_unames), 7z (signature_version, next_header_offset), rar (version), iso (primary_volume_id, system_id, volume_creation_date, publisher_id). Headers only.\"},\n333\t  {\"id\": \"x509-cert\", \"concept\": \"X.509 subject/issuer/serial/validity/fingerprint\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt x509 (alias cert), fields subject_cn, issuer_cn, serial_hex, not_before_utc, not_after_utc, sha256_fingerprint, sha1_fingerprint, san_dns_names. Shares the DER walker with pe-authenticode; cryptography needs the allowlist.\"},\n334\t  {\"id\": \"sqlite-header\", \"concept\": \"SQLite header + table names + browser history\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt sqlite, fields page_size, text_encoding, user_version, application_id_u32_hex, table_names, page_count. Header is pure struct; table names via sqlite_master page-1 b-tree walk (stdlib), or allowlist sqlite3 (`connect(':memory:').deserialize(b)`, Py3.12 has it).\"},\n335\t  {\"id\": \"tool-mutagen-pypdf\", \"concept\": \"Media tag + PDF python libs for the worker\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"mutagen 1.48, pypdf, exifread, soundfile are in .venv now (worker-side). Still missing: pymediainfo, PyAV. See tool-ffprobe for the media ground truth.\"},\n336\t  {\"id\": \"tool-dfir-parsers\", \"concept\": \"Prefetch / MFT / MSG / archive libs\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install dissect.util (LZXpress Huffman for Win10 prefetch), python-registry, extract_msg, py7zr, rarfile, pycdlib, analyzeMFT, windowsprefetch. apt: genisoimage (isoinfo), libscca-utils (sccainfo), osslsigncode.\"},\n337\t  {\"id\": \"media-tags\", \"concept\": \"MP4 mvhd / ID3 / WAV INFO / FLAC Vorbis\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT as fmt wav/mp3 only (D17 GM used fmt `media`, so these were invisible) -- see media-fmt-alias. Remaining: mp4 (ftyp_major_brand, mvhd_creation_time_utc, duration_seconds) and flac (streaminfo_sample_rate, vorbis_<tag>) modules -- now covered by media-stream-fields / flac-opus-headers / media-format-tags.\"},\n338\t  {\"id\": \"flac-opus-headers\", \"concept\": \"FLAC STREAMINFO / OpusHead / Vorbis identification header fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (+flac/ogg/opus aliases), fields flac_min_block_size, flac_max_block_size, flac_sample_rate, flac_channels, flac_bits_per_sample, flac_total_samples, flac_md5_signature (32 hex, 'none' when all zero), flac_metadata_block_types, opus_version, opus_channel_count, opus_pre_skip, opus_input_sample_rate, opus_output_gain, opus_channel_mapping_family, vorbis_bitrate_nominal, vorbis_blocksizes, ogg_serial_numbers_hex, ogg_page_count, ogg_last_granule. Pure struct.\"},\n339\t  {\"id\": \"video-color-timing\", \"concept\": \"Video color / timing fields (color_*, field_order, has_b_frames, VFR, start_time)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (+video/av). ffprobe names: color_range (`tv`/`pc` from VUI video_full_range_flag or colr nclx full-range bit), color_space (`bt709`, `smpte170m`, `bt2020nc`), color_transfer (`bt709`, `smpte2084`, `arib-std-b67`), color_primaries; field_order (`progressive` when frame_mbs_only_flag, else `tt`/`bb` best-effort), has_b_frames (h264: SPS VUI max_num_reorder_frames else 2 for High with ctts, 0 Baseline), avg_frame_rate (nb_frames / duration reduced) vs r_frame_rate (D18 `10/1`), is_variable_frame_rate (stts deltas differ), start_time (elst media_time / timescale, ffprobe `0.000000`), primary_video_duration (6 decimals), primary_video_bit_rate (btrt avgBitrate else sum(stsz)*8/duration), nb_frames (stsz count; D18 5). Fixtures: D18 mp4 + hand-packed colr box.\"},\n340\t  {\"id\": \"elf-hardening-checksec\", \"concept\": \"ELF hardening flags (PIE, NX, RELRO, canary, FORTIFY)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt elf: pie (ET_DYN with PT_INTERP or DF_1_PIE -> true), nx (PT_GNU_STACK present and !PF_X), relro (`none`/`partial`/`full`: PT_GNU_RELRO + DT_BIND_NOW or DF_1_NOW), canary (`__stack_chk_fail` in dynsym), fortify (`__*_chk` imports), executable_stack, textrel. Booleans `true`/`false`. Fixture: day19 elf (ET_EXEC -> pie false).\"},\n341\t  {\"id\": \"go-rust-buildinfo\", \"concept\": \"Go buildinfo / build ID and Rust toolchain provenance inside ELF/PE/Mach-O\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt go (aliases golang, elf, pe, macho): find `\\\\xff Go buildinf:` (16-B header; ptr size @14, flags @15; flags&2 -> inline varint-prefixed strings: Go version `go1.22.3`, then modinfo text with `path`, `mod`, `dep`, `build\\\\tGOOS=linux`, `build\\\\tGOARCH=arm64`, `-ldflags`, `vcs.revision`, `vcs.time`); fields go_version, module_path, main_module_version, goos, goarch, build_settings (JSON object), vcs_revision, go_build_id (`\\\\xff Go build ID: \\\"...\\\"` / ELF note `.note.go.buildid` type 4 'Go'). Rust: rustc_version from `.comment` `rustc version 1.xx.y (hash date)`, rustc_commit from `/rustc/<40 hex>/library` paths. Fixtures: day09-11 Go PE (pe-base-<goarch>.exe).\"},\n342\t  {\"id\": \"bytecode-headers\", \"concept\": \"Java class / .pyc / WASM / DEX headers (and the cafebabe Mach-O-fat collision)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt java (alias class/jvm): magic_u32_hex `0xcafebabe`, minor_version, major_version (52=Java 8, 55=11, 61=17, 65=21), java_version, constant_pool_count, this_class name, access_flags_u16_hex. Disambiguate from Mach-O fat (u32 BE @4: fat nfat_arch small; class minor<<16|major with major>=45). fmt pyc: magic_u16 (LE) -> python_version table (3.8 3413, 3.9 3425, 3.10 3439, 3.11 3495, 3.12 3531, 3.13 3571), flags_u32_hex, source_mtime_utc, source_size. fmt wasm: version_u32, section_ids/custom_section_names/export_names (JSON). fmt dex: version (`035`/`039`), checksum_u32_hex (adler32), signature_sha1_hex, file_size, string_ids_size, class_defs_size.\"},\n343\t  {\"id\": \"linux-packages\", \"concept\": \"Linux deployment packages: .deb / .rpm / AppImage / squashfs headers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 'rebuild deployment groups'. fmt deb: ar `!<arch>\\\\n` members (60-B headers) debian-binary (`2.0`), control.tar.{gz,xz,zst} -> ./control Package/Version/Architecture/Maintainer/Depends, member_names (ar order); fmt rpm: lead `ed ab ee db` (type u16 @6, archnum u16 @8, name 66 B @10), header `8e ad e8 01` index entries -> NAME 1000, VERSION 1001, RELEASE 1002, ARCH 1022, OS 1021, PAYLOADCOMPRESSOR 1125; fmt appimage: ELF with `AI\\\\x02` @8, squashfs offset = end of ELF sections; fmt squashfs: `hsqs` superblock inode count, mkfs_time_utc, block_size, compression id (1 gzip 2 lzma 3 lzo 4 xz 5 lz4 6 zstd), version. zstd not in stdlib -> `none` for zstd-only fields.\"},\n344\t  {\"id\": \"bplist-macos\", \"concept\": \"Apple property lists (binary/XML) and macOS artifacts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt plist (aliases bplist, macos): parse `bplist00` (trailer last 32 B: offset size, ref size, num objects, top object, offset table; types int/real/date(2001 epoch)/data/ascii/utf16/uid/array/dict) and XML plists (plistlib.loads is stdlib -- allowed? if not, hand-parse). Fields: top_level_keys (JSON, stored order), value_<key> (path with `/` for nesting), cf_bundle_identifier, cf_bundle_executable, cf_bundle_short_version_string, ls_minimum_system_version, object_count. Covers Info.plist next to Mach-O (D-lane macho prebuilt) and .webloc (`URL`).\"},\n345\t  {\"id\": \"msix-appx-arch\", \"concept\": \"MSIX/AppX packages and bundles: Identity incl. ProcessorArchitecture, bundle package list\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Windows-side 'fleet' analog. fmt msix (aliases appx, appxbundle, msixbundle): zip with `AppxManifest.xml` (or `AppxMetadata/AppxBundleManifest.xml`); xml.etree local-name. Fields: identity_name, identity_publisher, identity_version, identity_processor_architecture (`x64`/`x86`/`arm64`/`neutral` verbatim), target_device_families (JSON `Name MinVersion` stored order), bundle_package_architectures (JSON per <Package Architecture=> stored order), bundle_package_file_names, executable (Applications/Application@Executable), capabilities (JSON names stored order), signature_present (`AppxSignature.p7x`), block_map_hash_method (AppxBlockMap.xml HashMethod). Non-package -> `none`.\"},\n346\t  {\"id\": \"cpio-payloads\", \"concept\": \"cpio archives (newc/odc/binary) and Apple pbzx payloads\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt cpio (aliases payload, initramfs): newc `070701`/crc `070702` (110-B ASCII-hex header: ino mode uid gid nlink mtime filesize devmajor devminor rdevmajor rdevminor namesize check; name + data 4-byte aligned), odc `070707` (76-B octal), binary `c7 71`/`71 c7` (26-B, endian by magic); stop at `TRAILER!!!`. Fields: format (`newc`/`crc`/`odc`/`bin`), member_names (archive order, `TRAILER!!!` excluded), member_count, member_modes (octal string `0100755`), member_mtimes_utc, member_sizes, member_cpu_type_set / member_e_machine_set for embedded binaries. pbzx (`pbzx` magic, u64 BE flags then chunks of u64 decompressed/compressed size + XZ data) -> lzma.decompress chunks -> cpio. gzip/xz-wrapped cpio: decompress first. Non-cpio -> `none`.\"},\n347\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-bundle-clickonce\", \"concept\": \".NET deployment packaging: single-file bundle manifest, runtimeconfig/deps.json, ClickOnce entryPoint\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt dotnet_bundle (aliases singlefile, apphost): find the 32-B bundle marker (dotnet/runtime `bundle_marker` SHA-256 bytes `8b 12 02 b9 6a 61 20 38 72 7b 93 02 14 d7 a0 32 13 f5 b9 e6 ef ae 33 18 ee 3b 2d ce 24 b3 6a ae` -- verify against the runtime source) preceded by a u64 LE header offset; header = major/minor u32, file count i32, bundle id (7-bit-len string), [v2+: deps/runtimeconfig offsets+sizes, flags u64], then entries (offset i64, size i64, [compressed size i64 v6+], type u8, path string). Fields: bundle_version, bundle_id, file_names (JSON), file_count, main_assembly (first type-1 assembly matching the apphost name), runtimeconfig_tfm / framework_name / framework_version (JSON in the bundle or a `*.runtimeconfig.json` member). fmt clickonce (`.application`/`.manifest` XML ns urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v1/v2): entry_point_command_file, entry_point_parameters, assembly_identity_name/version/public_key_token/processor_architecture, deployment_provider_codebase.\"},\n348\t  {\"id\": \"apk-zip-structure\", \"concept\": \"APK/JAR zip-level forensics: signing-block offset, alignment, duplicate/hidden entries, LFH vs CD mismatches\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt apk (+jar): cd_offset_u32_hex, signing_block_offset_u32_hex, eocd_comment_length, lfh_cd_name_mismatches (JSON), lfh_cd_method_mismatches, stored_entry_names, compressed_manifest (AndroidManifest method != 0), data_after_eocd_bytes, extra_field_ids_by_entry (zipalign pads with 0xd935 'Android alignment' extra), general_purpose_flags_union_u16_hex (encrypted bit trick 0x0001 on a non-encrypted APK = anti-analysis), entry_count_eocd vs entry_count_cd. Pure struct over PK\\\\x03\\\\x04 / PK\\\\x01\\\\x02 / PK\\\\x05\\\\x06.\"},\n349\t  {\"id\": \"android-backup-artifacts\", \"concept\": \"Android device artifacts: `.ab` backups, OBB, packages.xml / packages.list\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt android_backup (alias ab): text header `ANDROID BACKUP\\\\n<version>\\\\n<compressed 0/1>\\\\n<encryption none|AES-256>\\\\n` then (zlib) tar with `apps/<pkg>/_manifest` (package, versionCode, platform version, signatures); fields backup_version, compressed, encryption, package_names (tar order), file_count. fmt packages_xml: ABX binary XML (`ABX\\\\0` magic, Android 12+) or text `<packages>`: package names, codePath, versionCode, installer, firstInstallTime (hex ms) -> utc; packages.list: name uid debuggable dataDir seinfo. fmt obb: zip/jobb footer.\"},\n350\t  {\"id\": \"mobileprovision-entitlements\", \"concept\": \"Standalone `.mobileprovision` / entitlements plists / iOS app extension Info.plists\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt mobileprovision (alias provisioning_profile): CMS DER with an embedded XML plist (find `<?xml`..`</plist>`): team_identifier, team_name, app_id_name, application_identifier, uuid, name, creation_date_utc, expiration_date_utc, provisions_all_devices, provisioned_device_count, provisioned_devices (JSON stored order), entitlement_keys (sorted), get_task_allow, aps_environment, developer_certificate_sha1s (DER certs in DeveloperCertificates <data> base64 -> sha1 hex). Shares code with ios-ipa-identity; register also as ipa provision_* fields.\"},\n351\t  {\"id\": \"disk-image-headers\", \"concept\": \"Virtual disk headers (VHD/VHDX/VMDK/QCOW2)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt vhd (footer `conectix` in the last 512 B, or first 512 for dynamic copies): creator_application (4 chars), creator_version_u32_hex, creator_host_os, original_size_bytes, current_size_bytes, disk_type (2 fixed,3 dynamic,4 differencing), timestamp_utc (seconds since 2000-01-01), unique_id_guid, checksum_u32_hex. vhdx `vhdxfile` creator UTF-16 string @8. vmdk: sparse header `KDMV` + embedded descriptor text -> create_type, cid, parent_cid, ddb_uuid, ddb_virtual_hw_version, adapter_type, extent_files. qcow2 `QFI\\\\xfb`: version, size_bytes, backing_file_name, cluster_bits, crypt_method. fmt `disk` alias.\"},\n352\t  {\"id\": \"ics-vcard-v2\", \"concept\": \"iCalendar / vCard fields (re-attempt; previous run failed on `import zoneinfo`)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Same scope as the given-up `ics-vcard` gap but with NO zoneinfo/dateutil import: fmt ics (ical, calendar): uid, organizer (verbatim incl. `mailto:`), attendees (JSON stored order), dtstart, dtend (verbatim value, plus _utc only when the value ends in Z), summary, location, method, prodid, event_count; fmt vcard (vcf): fn, n, email (first), emails, tel, org, uid, version. RFC 5545 unfolding (CRLF + space/tab), `KEY;PARAM=..:value` split on the first unquoted colon, unescape `\\\\,` `\\\\;` `\\\\n`.\"},\n353\t  {\"id\": \"tnef-winmail\", \"concept\": \"TNEF winmail.dat attachments\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt tnef (alias winmail): signature_u32_hex (0x223e9f78), key_u16, message_class, attachment_names (attAttachTitle 0x00018010), attachment_count, attachment_sizes_bytes. Level/attr id/len/data/checksum walk.\"},\n354\t  {\"id\": \"pcap-header\", \"concept\": \"PCAP/PCAPNG global header, linktype, packet count, interfaces\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt pcap / pcapng, fields magic_u32_hex, version, linktype, snaplen, packet_count, first_packet_time_utc, if_names (pcapng IDB if_name option 2), shb_os. Pure struct.\"},\n355\t  {\"id\": \"rtf-onenote\", \"concept\": \"RTF \\\\objdata OLE1 objects, OneNote embedded files\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt rtf: object_class_names, object_count, template_target, info_author; fmt onenote: embedded_file_count, embedded_file_sha256s. Hex-decode \\\\objdata, OLE1 header (class name len-prefixed).\"},\n356\t  {\"id\": \"msitools-path\", \"concept\": \"msitools present but not on PATH\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"tools/msitools/usr/bin/{msiinfo,msidump,msiextract,gcab} exist but `source bin/env.sh` doesn't expose them; add a bin/ shim. reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md still says 'Not installed: msitools, LnkParse3, dnfile' -- all three are now present (LnkParse3 + dnfile in .venv).\"},\n357\t  {\"id\": \"elf-core-ko-firmware\", \"concept\": \"ELF relocatables / kernel modules / core dumps and firmware image headers\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt elf: modinfo_<key> from `.modinfo` NUL-separated `key=value` (vermagic, srcversion, license, name, depends, author); core dumps (e_type 4): NT_PRPSINFO pr_fname/pr_psargs, NT_FILE mapped paths JSON, NT_PRSTATUS count (threads), NT_AUXV AT_EXECFN. fmt uimage: U-Boot legacy `27 05 19 56` BE header: hcrc/dcrc_u32_hex, time_utc, size, load/entry_u32_hex, os/arch/type/comp names, image_name (32 B NUL-trimmed).\"}\n358\t]\n359\t```"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ddb5173e-94e5-457f-8948-334914a57ded","uuid":"363aeea6-1311-4e3c-9813-0a14aba8853c","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:31:23.823Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md","content":"## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n\n```\n4d 5a (MZ) .. \"PE\\0\\0\"@e_lfanew  