 \"detail\": \"D23 flavor 'connect databases to parent applications'. New module lib/meta/prebuilt/sqlite_apps.py, fmt sqlite: application_id_u32_hex (exists -- reuse), application_id_ascii (4 printable bytes BE, D23 `HTRT`), application_id_known_name (registered ids: 0x0f055112/0x0f055113 Fossil, 0x47504b47 `GPKG`, 0x47503130 `GP10`, 0x4d504258 MBTiles, 0x5a4b4d42?? -- only well-documented ones from sqlite's magic.txt), parent_application (schema fingerprint table -> name: Chrome History {urls, visits, downloads, keyword_search_terms}, Chrome Cookies {cookies, meta}, Chrome Login Data {logins}, Chrome Web Data {autofill}, Firefox places {moz_places, moz_historyvisits}, Firefox cookies {moz_cookies}, Firefox formhistory {moz_formhistory}, Safari History.db {history_items, history_visits}, iMessage chat.db {message, handle, chat}, iOS sms.db, Android mmssms.db {sms, pdu}, contacts2.db {raw_contacts}, WhatsApp msgstore.db {messages, jid}, Windows ActivitiesCache.db {Activity, ActivityOperation}, Windows wpndatabase.db {Notification, NotificationHandler}, Skype main.db {Messages, Conversations}; else `unknown`), meta_version / meta_last_compatible_version (Chrome `meta` table key/value rows), user_version (exists), table_fingerprint (sorted user table names JSON). Reuse sqlite.py's stdlib schema walker (import its helpers). Synthesis helper: databases grouped by parent_application (JSON object app -> sorted names).\"},\n {\"id\": \"ese-edb-header\", \"concept\": \"ESE / JET Blue database header (SRUM, WebCacheV01.dat, Windows.edb, ntds.dit) -- next 'application database' family\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"fmt ese (aliases edb, esedb, jet, srum). Header page 0 (LE): checksum u32 @0, signature `ef cd ab 89` @4, format_version u32 @8 (0x620), file_type u32 @12 (0 database, 1 streaming), database_time (8 B) @16, database_signature (28 B: random u32 + log time 8 B + computer name 16 B) @24, database_state u32 @52 (1 JustCreated, 2 DirtyShutdown, 3 CleanShutdown, 4 BeingConverted, 5 ForceDetach) -> state name spelling `clean_shutdown`/`dirty_shutdown` + raw int, format_revision u32 @232, page_size u32 @236 (4096/8192/16384/32768), creation_format_version @216?, repair_count, last_attach/detach times (log time = 6 B y/m/d/h/m/s bytes + padding -> ISO-8601), shadow header copy at page 1 (compare -> header_shadow_match). Fields: page_size_bytes, format_version_u32_hex, format_revision_u32_hex, database_state, database_state_name, file_type, page_count (len // page_size - 2 header pages? emit len // page_size), is_dirty. Catalog (table names) only if a stdlib page walk fits in ~200 lines: catalog root = page 4 (FDP 2) -> table names MSysObjects, SruDbIdMapTable, {D10CA2FE-...} SRUM GUID tables, Containers (WebCache) -> table_names JSON sorted. Non-ESE -> `none`. Fixtures: synthesize headers with struct (no Windows DB here); `esedbinfo` is missing.\"},\n {\"id\": \"leveldb-indexeddb\", \"concept\": \"LevelDB / Chromium IndexedDB / Local Storage files (Electron & Chrome app data)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"fmt leveldb (aliases ldb, indexeddb, local_storage). Table file (`*.ldb`/`*.sst`): 48-B footer at EOF = metaindex BlockHandle + index BlockHandle (varint64 pairs) + padding + magic `57 fb 80 8b 24 75 47 db` (LE 0xdb4775248b80fb57); blocks: entries (shared varint, non_shared varint, value_len varint, key delta, value) + restart array + 5-B trailer (compression type 0 none / 1 snappy + crc32c masked). Log file (`*.log`, `MANIFEST-*`): 32 KiB blocks of records {crc32c u32, length u16, type u8 FULL1/FIRST2/MIDDLE3/LAST4}; WriteBatch = seq u64 + count u32 + (tag 1 put klen key vlen value / 0 delete). MANIFEST VersionEdit tags: 1 comparator (`leveldb.BytewiseComparator`, Chrome IndexedDB `idb_cmp1`), 2 log number, 3 next file, 4 last sequence, 7 new file (level, number, size, smallest, largest). `CURRENT` text = `MANIFEST-000001\\\\n`. Fields: file_kind (`table`/`log`/`manifest`/`current`), table_magic_u64_hex, block_compression (`snappy`/`none`), comparator_name, last_sequence, log_record_count, put_count, delete_count, keys (JSON stored order, printable or hex), value_for_key_<k>, local_storage_origins (Chromium `_https://site\\\\x00\\\\x01key` -> sorted origins), indexeddb_database_names. Snappy: hand-written decoder (~50 lines, stdlib) -- the python-snappy module is not allowlisted.\"},\n {\"id\": \"sqlite-embedded-carve\", \"concept\": \"SQLite embedded in or mislabeled as another file (magic at a non-zero offset)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"D23 flavor 'copied, truncated, embedded, and mislabeled'. fmt sqlite: make every sqlite.* field fall back to the FIRST `SQLite format 3\\\\0` occurrence when @0 is not the magic only for fields named embedded_* (keep the @0-or-`none` rule for plain fields -- a decoy must still answer `none`): embedded_offset (decimal), embedded_offset_hex, embedded_count (all header hits whose page size is valid), embedded_page_size_bytes, embedded_carved_length (in-header pages x page size, clipped to EOF), embedded_sha256 (of the carved bytes), host_magic_prefix_hex_16 (the first 16 bytes of the container), declared_extension_matches (extension of the member name vs `sqlite/db/sqlite3/sqlitedb`). Also teach lib member resolution to treat `x.zip -> app.apk -> assets/data.db` and PE overlay carving. Fixtures: day23 db appended to a PNG and to a PE stub; plain day23 db (offset 0).\"},\n {\"id\": \"sqlite-wal-journal\", \"concept\": \"SQLite WAL / rollback-journal / shm sidecar files\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"fmt sqlite_wal (aliases wal, sqlite) and sqlite_journal (alias journal). WAL: 32-B header BE: magic u32 0x377f0682 (LE checksums) / 0x377f0683 (BE), format version u32 @4 (3007000), page size u32 @8, checkpoint sequence @12, salt-1 @16, salt-2 @20, checksum-1/2 @24/@28; frames = 24-B header {page number u32, db size after commit u32 (non-zero = commit frame), salt1, salt2, cksum1, cksum2} + page. Fields: wal_page_size_bytes, wal_format_version, checkpoint_sequence, salt1_u32_hex, salt2_u32_hex, frame_count ((len-32)//(24+ps)), commit_frame_count, valid_frame_count (salts match header AND cumulative checksum chain valid -- implement the sqlite wal checksum: s0 += x0 + s1; s1 += x1 + s0 over u32 pairs in the magic's byte order), pages_written (sorted unique JSON), last_commit_db_size_pages. Rollback journal: magic `d9 d5 05 f9 20 a1 63 d7`, page count u32 @8 (-1 = compute), nonce @12, initial db size pages @16, sector size @20, page size @24 -> journal_page_count, journal_page_size_bytes, journal_sector_size. shm: wal-index header version 3007000 @0, mxFrame @16, nPage @20. Non-matching -> `none`.\"},\n {\"id\": \"browser-profile-dbs\", \"concept\": \"Browser profile SQLite stores beyond history: cookies, logins, autofill, downloads\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"Extend fmt sqlite (+ aliases chrome, firefox, browser) in lib/meta/prebuilt/sqlite_browser.py reusing sqlite.py's walker: Chrome Cookies (cookies: host_key, name, path, creation_utc/expires_utc/last_access_utc WebKit us since 1601 -> ISO-8601 Z, is_secure, is_httponly, samesite, encrypted_value prefix `v10`/`v11`/`v20` -> cookie_encryption_version) -> cookie_hosts (sorted unique), cookie_count, cookie_names; Chrome Login Data (logins: origin_url, action_url, username_value, date_created) -> login_origins, login_usernames; Web Data (autofill name/value/count/date_last_used); History downloads (target_path, tab_url, referrer, danger_type, total_bytes, start_time) -> download_target_paths, download_urls (downloads_url_chains); Firefox cookies.sqlite moz_cookies (host, name, expiry s, lastAccessed us), formhistory.sqlite moz_formhistory (fieldname, value, timesUsed), places moz_bookmarks titles. All lists sorted unless the question says order; timestamps ISO-8601 `Z` second precision (+ raw int sibling).\"},\n {\"id\": \"mobile-app-dbs\", \"concept\": \"Mobile app SQLite databases (iOS sms.db / KnowledgeC, Android mmssms / contacts2, WhatsApp msgstore)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"fmt sqlite (+ aliases ios, android, whatsapp) in lib/meta/prebuilt/sqlite_mobile.py: iOS sms.db/chat.db (message: text, date = ns since 2001-01-01 when > 1e12 else s, is_from_me, service iMessage/SMS; handle.id) -> message_count, handle_ids (sorted), first/last_message_utc, services; KnowledgeC.db ZOBJECT (ZSTREAMNAME `/app/inFocus`, ZVALUESTRING bundle id, ZSTARTDATE Cocoa s) -> app_bundle_ids; Android mmssms.db sms (address, date ms since 1970, type 1 inbox / 2 sent, body) -> sms_count, sms_addresses; contacts2.db raw_contacts/data display names; WhatsApp msgstore.db (messages / message table: key_remote_jid, timestamp ms, data) -> chat_jids, message_count. Timestamps ISO-8601 `Z`. Missing table -> `none`.\"},\n {\"id\": \"sqlite-deleted-records\", \"concept\": \"Deleted / unallocated SQLite content: freelist pages, freeblocks, carved rows\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"fmt sqlite: freelist_trunk_pages (JSON chain order from @32), freelist_leaf_pages (sorted), freelist_page_count_walked vs header @36 (freelist_count_mismatch), freeblock_count (sum over table leaf pages: first freeblock u16 @1 of the b-tree page header, chain next u16 / size u16), unallocated_bytes (cell content start @5 minus end of cell pointer array), carved_strings (printable UTF-8 runs >= 6 from freeblocks + freelist leaf pages, JSON sorted unique), deleted_row_candidates (best-effort record-header parse at each freeblock offset +4: serial types -> values, JSON list of lists). secure_delete hint: freelist pages all-zero -> `true`. Stdlib only.\"},\n {\"id\": \"other-app-db-formats\", \"concept\": \"Other application database formats: MS Access Jet/ACE, dBase .dbf, Berkeley DB, LMDB, Realm\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"Separate fmts, header fields only, magic-gated (else `none`). access (aliases mdb, accdb, jet): `00 01 00 00` + `Standard Jet DB`/`Standard ACE DB` @4, version u32 @0x14 (0 Jet3, 1 Jet4, 2 ACE12, 3 ACE14, 5 ACE16/17) -> version_name, page_size (2048 Jet3 / 4096), database_password_masked (RC4-obfuscated header; report `none`). dbf (alias dbase): version byte @0 (0x03 dBase III, 0x30 VFP, 0x83 with memo, 0x8b dBase IV memo), last_update `YYYY-MM-DD` (YY @1 + 1900, MM @2, DD @3), record_count u32 LE @4, header_size u16 @8, record_size u16 @10, field_names (32-B descriptors from @32 until 0x0D: name[11] NUL-trimmed, type char @11, length @16) JSON stored order. bdb (alias berkeleydb): magic u32 @12 (0x00061561 hash, 0x00053162 btree, 0x00042253 queue, 0x00040988 log) in either byte order -> db_type, version u32 @16, pagesize u32 @20, byte_order. lmdb: meta page magic 0xBEEFC0DE @16 (LE), version @20, map size, last txn id. realm: `T-DB` @16, file format version @22/@23, top refs @0/@8.\"},\n]\ngaps = [g for g in gaps] + new\ngaps.sort(key=lambda g: g['priority'])  # stable: keeps relative order within a priority\nhdr = (\"Ranking (D23 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D24-D26 question with no extractor or a lane-wide failure mode:\\n\"\n       \"the D23 'application databases' flavor siblings (truncation / impossible header claims, parent-app attribution,\\n\"\n       \"embedded copies) and the NEXT application-data families (ESE/JET, LevelDB/IndexedDB), plus the timed carry-over\\n\"\n       \"mutation rules (json lists SORTED). The D22 JAR/launcher items dropped to 2 (built; every family since D17 lasted\\n\"\n       \"one day). TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail` for prebuild items.\\n\\n\")\nbody = '[\\n' + ',\\n'.join('  ' + json.dumps(g, ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps) + '\\n]'\njson.loads(body)\nt = t[:m.start()] + m.group(1) + '\\n' + hdr + m.group(3) + body + m.group(5) + t[m.end():]\nopen(F, 'w').write(t)\nPYEOF\npython3 -I $TMPDIR/upd_gaps.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\nt=open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md').read()\nj=json.loads(re.search(r'## Readiness gaps.*?```json\\n(.*?)\\n```',t,re.S).group(1))\ns=json.load(open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/.run/prebuild-state.json'))\nids=[g['id'] for g in j]; assert len(ids)==len(set(ids))\nassert all(set(g)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for g in j)\npend=[g['id'] for g in j if g['action']=='prebuild' and not (s.get('metadata-forensics:'+g['id'],{}).get('ok') or s.get('metadata-forensics:'+g['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(j), 'pending', len(pend), pend)\nprint([ (g['priority'],g['id']) for g in j][:10])\nEOF\nsed -n '/^## Readiness gaps/,/^```json/p' reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md","description":"Rewrite readiness gaps and validate JSON"}}}
