{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKFzsgsGbayCYGRQYbzW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I updated both lane files and nothing else. The technique log is 234 lines, slightly over the ~200 target.\n\n1. **`reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md`**: added the day23 entry. \"Page Me Maybe\" asked for `sqlite.page_size_bytes`, a 2-byte big-endian value at offset 16 of the SQLite header, where a stored `1` means 65536. The prebuilt `sqlite.py` answered it in the race probe, correct in about 29 s with no wrong submits. The bigger news is in the timed modes:\n   - **Every carried field changed value**, including ones that had been constant since day13: Mach-O became multi-slice (fat), PE/ELF had non-x86 machine types, audio came as MP3/Opus/Vorbis, and the zip directory order was shuffled.\n   - **List order:** the GM rejected zip member names in on-disk order and accepted them sorted. Earlier zips were already stored sorted, so the old \"keep directory order\" rule had never actually been tested. The new rule is that every JSON list answer is sorted ascending, except the synthesis question, which is ordered by digest.\n   - **Python repr:** a list was once emitted as a Python repr instead of compact JSON.\n\n   Time Trial lost one submit to the order problem. Mastery's single GM submit was correct after the pre-submit check caught both issues and three offline fix-up runs, which matches the \"had trouble\" flag. I put the order rule, the repr rule and all the changed values under Variant axes, Conventions, Recognition cues and Pitfalls, and shortened the day15-22 entries.\n2. **`reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md`**: marked SQLite page size `seen D23` and dropped the `sqlite-header` gap. I corrected the zip member-names and Mach-O rows to \"sorted\", added nine new concept rows, rewrote the forecast for the shift from runnable formats to application data, and kept the Recognition cues section at exactly 60 lines.\n3. **Readiness gaps**: re-ranked so priority 1 covers the unasked day23 flavor (truncation and \"impossible claim\" checks, linking a database to its parent app, embedded copies), the likely next database formats (ESE/JET, LevelDB/IndexedDB), and a note on the timed changes. The day22 JAR items are already built and moved to priority 2. I added 10 new prebuild gaps; with the PyInstaller gap still pending after a failed first attempt, 11 are unbuilt. The JSON block parses, ids are unique, and the keys are unchanged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":612,"cache_read_input_tokens":182443,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":612},"output_tokens":724,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ddb5173e-94e5-457f-8948-334914a57ded","uuid":"a3358390-7f04-4749-b136-3709094a776e","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:37:25.749Z","request_id":"req_011CgKFzsJoHAskVouoMeqhw"}
